1
00:00:46,214 --> 00:00:49,467
(CELTIC FLUTE MUSIC PLAYING)

2
00:01:11,197 --> 00:01:12,448
(BIRDSONG)

3
00:01:18,788 --> 00:01:22,250
Where are you? Come out!

4
00:01:22,333 --> 00:01:24,418
Come out! (LAUGHS)

5
00:01:25,294 --> 00:01:27,255
Come on out.

6
00:01:27,338 --> 00:01:28,589
(GIGGLES)

7
00:01:28,673 --> 00:01:32,343
- I'm coming to get you.
- (GIGGLES)

8
00:01:33,636 --> 00:01:36,639
Where are you, you little rascal?
I'm coming to get you.

9
00:01:36,722 --> 00:01:38,683
Hm. (CHUCKLES)

10
00:01:38,766 --> 00:01:41,477
Where is my little birthday girl, hm?

11
00:01:42,353 --> 00:01:45,606
I'm going to gobble her up
when I find her.

12
00:01:45,690 --> 00:01:47,483
- Oh! (LAUGHS)
- (SQUEALS)

13
00:01:47,567 --> 00:01:49,527
I'm going to eat you. I am.

14
00:01:49,610 --> 00:01:51,571
(MAKES MUNCHING NOISES)

15
00:01:51,654 --> 00:01:55,116
Och, Fergus, no weapons on the table.

16
00:01:55,199 --> 00:01:57,410
Can I shoot an arrow?
Can I? Can I? Can I? Can I?

17
00:01:57,493 --> 00:01:59,704
Please? Can I? (LAUGHS)

18
00:01:59,787 --> 00:02:02,790
- Not with that. Why not...
- (GIGGLES)

19
00:02:02,873 --> 00:02:04,208
...use your very own?

20
00:02:04,292 --> 00:02:07,587
- (GASPS)
- Happy birthday, my wee darling!

21
00:02:08,212 --> 00:02:09,213
(BOW BEING PLUCKED)

22
00:02:11,465 --> 00:02:13,509
- Now, there's a good girl.
- (STRAINS)

23
00:02:13,593 --> 00:02:16,178
Draw all the way back now
to your cheek. That's right.

24
00:02:17,471 --> 00:02:19,473
Keep both eyes open.

25
00:02:20,433 --> 00:02:22,435
And, loose!

26
00:02:24,562 --> 00:02:26,564
- I missed.
- Go and fetch it, then.

27
00:02:28,899 --> 00:02:31,861
A bow, Fergus? She's a lady.

28
00:02:32,111 --> 00:02:33,988
- Ooh! You!
- (LAUGHS)

29
00:02:42,371 --> 00:02:44,665
(BIRDS CALLING)

30
00:02:57,511 --> 00:02:59,513
(CREAKING)

31
00:03:01,724 --> 00:03:03,601
(LONE BIRD CALLS)

32
00:03:04,435 --> 00:03:06,270
(HEAVY BREATHING)

33
00:03:08,189 --> 00:03:10,191
(HIGH-PITCHED CALL)

34
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:12,443
A will-o'-the-wisp.

35
00:03:15,112 --> 00:03:16,697
(GROWLING)

36
00:03:20,743 --> 00:03:22,870
They are real.

37
00:03:30,836 --> 00:03:33,422
ELINOR:
Merida, come along, sweetheart.

38
00:03:33,506 --> 00:03:35,675
- We're leaving now.
- MERIDA: I saw a wisp.

39
00:03:37,677 --> 00:03:39,762
- I saw a wisp.
- A wisp?

40
00:03:39,845 --> 00:03:45,184
You know, some say that
will-o'-the-wisps lead you to your fate.

41
00:03:45,267 --> 00:03:47,728
- Oh, aye. Or an arrow.
- Och!

42
00:03:47,812 --> 00:03:50,815
Come on, let's be off before we see
a dancing Tatty Bogle.

43
00:03:50,898 --> 00:03:53,317
Or a giant having a jigger
in the bluebells.

44
00:03:53,401 --> 00:03:55,277
Your father doesn't believe in magic.

45
00:03:55,361 --> 00:03:57,780
Well, he should. Because it's true.

46
00:03:57,863 --> 00:03:59,240
(GASPS)
(SCREAMS)

47
00:03:59,323 --> 00:04:00,741
(GROWLS)

48
00:04:00,825 --> 00:04:02,535
Mor'du! Elinor, run!

49
00:04:02,618 --> 00:04:04,578
- (ROARS)
- Sire!

50
00:04:04,662 --> 00:04:06,664
(YELLS)

51
00:04:09,792 --> 00:04:10,793
(SNARLS)

52
00:04:13,045 --> 00:04:14,088
Come on, you!

53
00:04:14,171 --> 00:04:15,172
(ROARS)

54
00:04:27,852 --> 00:04:30,980
MERIDA: <i>Some say our destiny
is tied to the land...</i>

55
00:04:32,022 --> 00:04:34,525
<i>...as much a part of us as we are of it.</i>

56
00:04:37,862 --> 00:04:41,699
<i>Others say fate is woven together
like a cloth.</i>

57
00:04:41,782 --> 00:04:43,242
(THUNDER RUMBLES)

58
00:04:43,325 --> 00:04:46,537
<i>So that one's destiny intertwines
with many others.</i>

59
00:04:50,749 --> 00:04:55,546
<i>It's the one thing we search for
or fight to change.</i>

60
00:04:57,339 --> 00:04:59,341
<i>Some never find it.</i>

61
00:05:01,594 --> 00:05:04,722
<i>But there are some who are led.</i>

62
00:05:09,643 --> 00:05:10,644
(YELLS)

63
00:05:10,728 --> 00:05:12,480
<i>The story of how my father lost his leg</i>

64
00:05:13,564 --> 00:05:14,857
<i>to the demon bear Mor'du
became legend.</i>

65
00:05:16,150 --> 00:05:17,318
(GROANING)

66
00:05:18,319 --> 00:05:20,821
<i>I became a sister to three new brothers.</i>

67
00:05:20,905 --> 00:05:23,908
<i>The princes.
Hamish, Hubert and Harris.</i>

68
00:05:24,575 --> 00:05:26,911
<i>Wee devils, more like.</i>

69
00:05:26,994 --> 00:05:29,497
<i>They get away with murder.</i>

70
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:31,832
<i>I can never get away with anything.</i>

71
00:05:33,792 --> 00:05:35,836
<i>I'm the princess.</i>

72
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:37,505
- Oh!
- (BAGPIPES PLAYING)

73
00:05:37,588 --> 00:05:39,590
MERIDA: <i>I'm the example.</i>

74
00:05:40,549 --> 00:05:41,550
(SLURPS)

75
00:05:41,634 --> 00:05:44,595
<i>I've got duties, responsibilities,
expectations.</i>

76
00:05:44,678 --> 00:05:46,472
<i>My whole life is planned out,</i>

77
00:05:46,555 --> 00:05:48,516
<i>preparing for the day I become...</i>

78
00:05:48,599 --> 00:05:50,017
<i>Well, my mother.</i>

79
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:52,937
<i>She's in charge
of every single day of my life.</i>

80
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:55,022
- (BAGPIPES CEASE)
- (SIGHS)

81
00:05:56,398 --> 00:05:59,860
"Aye, Robin, Jolly Robin,
and thou shalt know of mine."

82
00:05:59,944 --> 00:06:01,070
Project!

83
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:03,072
"And thou shalt know of mine!"

84
00:06:03,322 --> 00:06:06,700
Enunciate. You must be understood
from anywhere in the room,

85
00:06:06,784 --> 00:06:08,369
or it's all for naught.

86
00:06:08,452 --> 00:06:10,955
- This is all for naught.
- I heard that!

87
00:06:11,038 --> 00:06:12,540
- (SIGHS)
- From the top.

88
00:06:12,623 --> 00:06:15,584
A princess must be knowledgeable
about her kingdom.

89
00:06:17,127 --> 00:06:19,129
She does not doodle.

90
00:06:19,672 --> 00:06:21,674
(PLAYS NOTES)

91
00:06:21,757 --> 00:06:23,759
That's a C, dear.

92
00:06:26,428 --> 00:06:28,556
- (SCREECHES)
- (SCREAMS)

93
00:06:28,639 --> 00:06:30,391
(LAUGHS AND SNORTS)

94
00:06:30,474 --> 00:06:32,560
A princess does not chortle.

95
00:06:32,643 --> 00:06:34,687
- Mm!
- Does not stuff her gob!

96
00:06:34,770 --> 00:06:36,480
Rises early.

97
00:06:36,564 --> 00:06:38,357
- ...is compassionate...
- (CHICKEN SQUAWKS)

98
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:39,858
...patient, cautious,

99
00:06:39,942 --> 00:06:40,901
clean.

100
00:06:40,985 --> 00:06:47,992
And above all, a princess
strives for... Well, perfection.

101
00:06:49,618 --> 00:06:51,161
MERIDA: <i>But every once in a while,</i>

102
00:06:51,412 --> 00:06:56,000
<i>there's a day
when I don't have to be a princess.</i>

103
00:06:58,627 --> 00:07:01,088
<i>No lessons, no expectations.</i>

104
00:07:01,171 --> 00:07:03,507
<i>A day where anything can happen.</i>

105
00:07:05,092 --> 00:07:08,095
<i>A day I can change my fate.</i>

106
00:07:08,178 --> 00:07:09,388
Yah!

107
00:07:18,022 --> 00:07:20,024
(LIVELY MUSIC PLAYING)

108
00:07:20,232 --> 00:07:26,238
<i>When cold wind is a' calling,
and the sky is clear and bright</i>

109
00:07:26,322 --> 00:07:31,994
<i>Misty mountains sing and beckon,
lead me out into the light</i>

110
00:07:32,369 --> 00:07:35,289
<i>I will ride, I will fly</i>

111
00:07:35,372 --> 00:07:38,334
<i>Chase the wind and touch the sky</i>

112
00:07:38,417 --> 00:07:44,089
<i>I will fly
Chase the wind and touch the sky</i>

113
00:07:49,219 --> 00:07:51,221
Whoo-hoo!

114
00:07:58,395 --> 00:07:59,480
(EAGLE CALLS)

115
00:07:59,563 --> 00:08:05,569
<i>Where dark woods hide secrets
and mountains are fierce and bold</i>

116
00:08:05,653 --> 00:08:11,617
<i>Deep waters hold reflections
of times lost long ago</i>

117
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:15,663
<i>I will read every story,
take hold of my own dream</i>

118
00:08:15,746 --> 00:08:17,706
- Oh!
- (HORSE WHINNIES)

119
00:08:17,790 --> 00:08:20,876
<i>Be as strong as the seas are stormy</i>

120
00:08:20,959 --> 00:08:23,712
<i>And proud as an eagle's scream</i>

121
00:08:23,796 --> 00:08:26,757
<i>I will ride, I will fly</i>

122
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:29,760
<i>Chase the wind and touch the sky</i>

123
00:08:29,843 --> 00:08:35,599
<i>I will fly
Chase the wind and touch the sky</i>

124
00:08:44,191 --> 00:08:46,193
(SCREAMS EXCITEDLY)

125
00:08:46,276 --> 00:08:48,112
<i>And touch the sky</i>

126
00:08:48,195 --> 00:08:50,197
Whoo!

127
00:08:51,990 --> 00:08:53,409
<i>Chase the wind</i>

128
00:08:53,492 --> 00:08:56,495
<i>Chase the wind</i>

129
00:08:56,578 --> 00:09:01,750
<i>Touch the sky</i>

130
00:09:09,007 --> 00:09:10,134
(WHINNIES)

131
00:09:10,217 --> 00:09:13,512
I'm starving. You hungry too, Angus?

132
00:09:13,971 --> 00:09:14,972
Pfft!

133
00:09:15,055 --> 00:09:17,015
- Oats it is, then.
- (SNORTS)

134
00:09:19,226 --> 00:09:20,894
Good day, Princess.

135
00:09:20,978 --> 00:09:22,855
I cannot find the salt.
Where did you put it?

136
00:09:22,938 --> 00:09:25,190
It was over there a minute ago,
the last time I looked at it.

137
00:09:25,941 --> 00:09:30,904
And then, out of nowhere,
the biggest bear you've ever seen!

138
00:09:30,988 --> 00:09:34,116
His hide littered with the weapons
of fallen warriors.

139
00:09:34,199 --> 00:09:37,828
His face scarred with one dead eye.

140
00:09:38,620 --> 00:09:40,247
I drew my sword and...

141
00:09:40,330 --> 00:09:41,874
Whoosh!

142
00:09:41,957 --> 00:09:44,084
One swipe, his sword shattered.

143
00:09:44,168 --> 00:09:47,296
Then "chomp"! Dad's leg was clean off.

144
00:09:47,671 --> 00:09:50,048
Down the monster's throat it went.

145
00:09:50,132 --> 00:09:53,051
Oh, that's my favourite part.

146
00:09:53,135 --> 00:09:56,388
Mor'du has never been seen since,

147
00:09:56,513 --> 00:10:01,935
and is roaming the wilds
waiting his chance of revenge.

148
00:10:02,019 --> 00:10:04,521
- (ROARING)
- Let him return.

149
00:10:04,605 --> 00:10:06,648
I'll finish what I guddled in the first place.

150
00:10:06,732 --> 00:10:10,527
Merida, a princess does not place
her weapons on the table.

151
00:10:10,611 --> 00:10:13,781
Mum! It's just my bow.

152
00:10:13,864 --> 00:10:16,825
A princess should not have weapons
in my opinion.

153
00:10:16,909 --> 00:10:18,243
FERGUS: Leave her be.

154
00:10:18,535 --> 00:10:21,205
Princess or not,
learning to fight is essential.

155
00:10:21,288 --> 00:10:24,082
Mum?
You'll never guess what I did today.

156
00:10:24,166 --> 00:10:26,335
- Hm?
- I climbed the Crone's Tooth,

157
00:10:26,585 --> 00:10:27,878
and drank from the Fire Falls.

158
00:10:28,420 --> 00:10:29,797
Fire Falls?

159
00:10:29,880 --> 00:10:33,634
They say only the ancient kings
were brave enough to drink the fire.

160
00:10:33,717 --> 00:10:34,718
(LAUGHS)

161
00:10:34,802 --> 00:10:37,596
- What did you do, dear?
- Nothing, Mum.

162
00:10:37,679 --> 00:10:39,139
Hungry, aren't we?

163
00:10:39,223 --> 00:10:41,600
- Mum!
- You'll get dreadful collywobbles.

164
00:10:41,683 --> 00:10:44,645
Oh, Fergus, will you look at
your daughter's plate?

165
00:10:44,728 --> 00:10:46,688
- (DOGS BARKING)
- So what?

166
00:10:46,772 --> 00:10:49,316
- Oh, you great...
- Don't let them lick... (SIGHS)

167
00:10:49,566 --> 00:10:50,859
Boys, you're naughty.

168
00:10:51,276 --> 00:10:52,986
Don't just play with your haggis.

169
00:10:53,070 --> 00:10:55,823
- Urgh! (GAGGING)
- Och, how do you know you don't like it,

170
00:10:55,906 --> 00:10:57,991
if you won't try it?

171
00:10:58,075 --> 00:10:59,910
That's just a wee sheep's stomach.

172
00:10:59,993 --> 00:11:02,621
It's delicious. Mm! (SMACKS LIPS)

173
00:11:02,704 --> 00:11:04,998
- My lady.
- Thank you, Maudie.

174
00:11:05,082 --> 00:11:06,250
FERGUS: You're getting too big,
the two of you.

175
00:11:10,963 --> 00:11:12,256
ELINOR: Aha.

176
00:11:12,339 --> 00:11:14,675
From the Lords Macintosh,
Mac Guffin and Dingwall.

177
00:11:14,758 --> 00:11:16,134
Their responses, no doubt.

178
00:11:16,218 --> 00:11:17,719
Aye, aye!

179
00:11:17,803 --> 00:11:19,805
- FERGUS: Hey, hey! (LAUGHS)
- (MUNCHING LOUDLY)

180
00:11:20,681 --> 00:11:23,350
Stay out of my food,
you greedy mongrels.

181
00:11:24,017 --> 00:11:26,144
Chew on that, you manky dogs!

182
00:11:26,228 --> 00:11:28,272
- (FERGUS LAUGHS)
- Fergus?

183
00:11:30,816 --> 00:11:32,025
They've all accepted.

184
00:11:32,109 --> 00:11:34,111
(DOGS SLOBBERING)

185
00:11:34,778 --> 00:11:36,989
Who's accepted what, Mother?

186
00:11:37,072 --> 00:11:39,283
Boys, you are excused.

187
00:11:39,992 --> 00:11:41,034
(GIGGLING)

188
00:11:42,119 --> 00:11:43,245
- Oof!
- (DOGS BARKING)

189
00:11:43,912 --> 00:11:45,205
Hey! (LAUGHS)

190
00:11:46,164 --> 00:11:49,001
What did I do now?

191
00:11:49,084 --> 00:11:51,295
Your father has something
to discuss with you.

192
00:11:53,797 --> 00:11:54,965
Fergus?

193
00:11:55,799 --> 00:11:57,676
Oh. (CLEARS THROAT)

194
00:11:57,759 --> 00:11:59,428
(COUGHS)

195
00:11:59,678 --> 00:12:02,890
Er... Merida.

196
00:12:05,934 --> 00:12:11,064
(SIGHS) The lords are presenting
their sons as suitors for your betrothal.

197
00:12:11,148 --> 00:12:13,984
- What?
- The clans have accepted.

198
00:12:14,651 --> 00:12:17,112
- Dad!
- What? (STAMMERS) I...

199
00:12:17,195 --> 00:12:19,364
You... She... Elinor?

200
00:12:19,448 --> 00:12:22,034
Honestly, Merida, I don't know why
you're reacting this way.

201
00:12:22,117 --> 00:12:23,076
(SIGHS IN FRUSTRATION)

202
00:12:23,160 --> 00:12:27,122
This year, each clan will present a suitor
to compete in the games for your hand.

203
00:12:27,205 --> 00:12:29,917
I suppose a princess
just does what she's told?

204
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:32,419
A princess does not raise her voice.

205
00:12:33,253 --> 00:12:36,298
Merida, this is what you've been
preparing for your whole life.

206
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:40,260
No, it's what you've been preparing
me for my whole life.

207
00:12:40,344 --> 00:12:42,679
I won't go through with it.
You can't make me.

208
00:12:42,763 --> 00:12:44,890
Merida!

209
00:12:45,098 --> 00:12:46,934
Huh? Merida!

210
00:12:49,686 --> 00:12:50,687
- Urgh!
- (DOGS BARKING)

211
00:12:50,771 --> 00:12:53,023
Boys!

212
00:12:53,982 --> 00:12:55,984
(GRUNTING)

213
00:12:57,194 --> 00:13:00,906
Mother. Suitors? Marriage?

214
00:13:00,989 --> 00:13:03,325
Once there was an ancient kingdom...

215
00:13:03,408 --> 00:13:06,036
Oh, Mum!

216
00:13:06,119 --> 00:13:07,746
Ancient kingdom.

217
00:13:07,829 --> 00:13:09,873
Its name long forgotten,

218
00:13:10,457 --> 00:13:14,461
ruled by a wise and fair king
who was much beloved.

219
00:13:14,962 --> 00:13:19,967
And when he grew old he divided
the kingdom among his four sons,

220
00:13:20,050 --> 00:13:24,429
that they should be the pillars
on which the peace of the land rested.

221
00:13:25,806 --> 00:13:30,811
But the oldest prince
wanted to rule the land for himself.

222
00:13:30,894 --> 00:13:34,481
He followed his own path
and the kingdom fell

223
00:13:35,774 --> 00:13:38,735
to war, and chaos and ruin.

224
00:13:38,819 --> 00:13:40,737
That's a nice story.

225
00:13:40,821 --> 00:13:43,073
It's not just a story, Merida.

226
00:13:43,156 --> 00:13:46,201
Legends are lessons.
They ring with truths.

227
00:13:46,284 --> 00:13:47,744
Och, Mum.

228
00:13:47,828 --> 00:13:49,997
I would advise you
to make your peace with this.

229
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:51,915
The clans are coming
to present their suitors.

230
00:13:51,999 --> 00:13:54,334
- It's not fair.
- Och, Merida.

231
00:13:54,418 --> 00:13:57,170
It's marriage.
It's not the end of the world.

232
00:13:58,255 --> 00:13:59,256
(SIGHS IN DISBELIEF)

233
00:14:01,216 --> 00:14:03,218
(ELINOR MUTTERING)

234
00:14:05,929 --> 00:14:08,640
- FERGUS: You're muttering.
- I don't mutter.

235
00:14:09,266 --> 00:14:12,561
Aye, you do. You mutter, lass,
when something's troubling you.

236
00:14:12,811 --> 00:14:14,855
I blame you. Stubbornness.

237
00:14:14,938 --> 00:14:16,565
It's entirely from your side of the family.

238
00:14:16,648 --> 00:14:19,526
(LAUGHS)
I take it the talk didn't go too well, then?

239
00:14:20,110 --> 00:14:22,112
Och, I don't know what to do.

240
00:14:22,195 --> 00:14:25,198
- Speak to her, dear.
- I do speak to her.

241
00:14:25,282 --> 00:14:28,577
- She just doesn't listen.
- Come on, now.

242
00:14:28,827 --> 00:14:31,204
Pretend I'm Merida. Speak to me.

243
00:14:31,288 --> 00:14:33,206
What would you say?

244
00:14:33,290 --> 00:14:35,792
Och... I can't do this.

245
00:14:35,876 --> 00:14:37,461
Sure you can.

246
00:14:37,544 --> 00:14:40,130
There, there. That's my queen.

247
00:14:40,213 --> 00:14:42,174
Right, here we go.

248
00:14:42,257 --> 00:14:43,967
"I don't want to get married.

249
00:14:44,051 --> 00:14:46,511
"I want to stay single
and let my hair flow in the wind

250
00:14:46,595 --> 00:14:50,515
"as I ride through the glen
firing arrows into the sunset."

251
00:14:53,477 --> 00:14:55,854
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

252
00:14:55,937 --> 00:15:00,901
Merida, all this work,
all the time spent preparing you,

253
00:15:00,984 --> 00:15:04,613
schooling you,
giving you everything we never had.

254
00:15:04,863 --> 00:15:08,325
I ask you, what do you expect us to do?

255
00:15:08,408 --> 00:15:11,495
Call off the gathering.
Would that kill them?

256
00:15:11,578 --> 00:15:12,913
You're the queen.

257
00:15:12,996 --> 00:15:16,291
You can just tell the lords
the princess is not ready for this.

258
00:15:16,374 --> 00:15:20,045
In fact, she might not ever be ready
for this, so that's that.

259
00:15:20,128 --> 00:15:24,174
Good day to you. We'll expect your
declarations of war in the morning.

260
00:15:24,257 --> 00:15:27,928
I understand this must all seem unfair.

261
00:15:28,011 --> 00:15:30,305
Even I had reservations
when I faced betrothal.

262
00:15:30,388 --> 00:15:33,892
But we can't just run away
from who we are.

263
00:15:33,975 --> 00:15:36,436
I don't want my life to be over.

264
00:15:36,520 --> 00:15:37,938
I want my freedom!

265
00:15:38,021 --> 00:15:41,274
But are you willing to pay the price
your freedom will cost?

266
00:15:41,358 --> 00:15:43,443
I'm not doing any of this to hurt you.

267
00:15:43,527 --> 00:15:49,074
If you could just try to see what I do,
I do out of love.

268
00:15:49,157 --> 00:15:52,119
But it's my life, it's... (SIGHS)

269
00:15:52,536 --> 00:15:54,287
I'm just not ready.

270
00:15:54,371 --> 00:15:56,248
I think you'd see, if you could just...

271
00:15:56,331 --> 00:15:59,376
I think I could make you understand
if you would just...

272
00:15:59,459 --> 00:16:01,044
- ...listen.
- ...listen.

273
00:16:01,128 --> 00:16:02,462
(WHINNIES)

274
00:16:04,381 --> 00:16:07,551
I swear, Angus,
this isn't going to happen.

275
00:16:08,552 --> 00:16:10,178
Not if I have any say in it.

276
00:16:12,097 --> 00:16:14,724
- (EXERTIVE GRUNTING)
- (DRUMS POUNDING)

277
00:16:16,977 --> 00:16:18,311
(MEN STRAINING)

278
00:16:22,315 --> 00:16:24,317
(DRUMS BEATING RHYTHMICALLY)

279
00:16:26,903 --> 00:16:28,488
Mac Guffin!

280
00:16:28,572 --> 00:16:30,073
MEN: Mac Guffin!

281
00:16:32,993 --> 00:16:34,995
- Dingwall!
- MEN: Dingwall!

282
00:16:36,705 --> 00:16:39,624
- Macintosh!
- MEN: Macintosh!

283
00:16:45,422 --> 00:16:47,424
Ooh! Aah!

284
00:16:48,008 --> 00:16:49,009
Oh.

285
00:16:50,302 --> 00:16:51,303
(SIGHS)

286
00:16:51,595 --> 00:16:52,554
(GRUNTS)

287
00:16:52,637 --> 00:16:56,099
You look absolutely beautiful.

288
00:16:56,183 --> 00:16:57,475
I can't breathe.

289
00:16:57,559 --> 00:16:59,561
Och, shush! Give us a turn.

290
00:17:01,021 --> 00:17:03,315
(GROANS) I can't move.

291
00:17:03,398 --> 00:17:05,442
It's too tight.

292
00:17:05,525 --> 00:17:08,278
- (STRAINS)
- It's perfect.

293
00:17:08,361 --> 00:17:10,280
(GROANS)

294
00:17:10,947 --> 00:17:12,616
(STRAINS)

295
00:17:20,665 --> 00:17:23,210
- Merida?
- Mum?

296
00:17:26,129 --> 00:17:28,131
Just...

297
00:17:30,759 --> 00:17:33,011
Remember to smile.

298
00:17:36,973 --> 00:17:38,975
(SNORING)

299
00:17:42,103 --> 00:17:44,105
(PRINCES LAUGHING)

300
00:17:46,566 --> 00:17:48,485
- (CONTINUES SNORING)
- Aye, they're coming.

301
00:17:48,568 --> 00:17:50,862
Places, everyone. Places.

302
00:17:50,946 --> 00:17:51,947
- (PEOPLE CLAMOURING)
- (DOGS BARKING)

303
00:17:53,240 --> 00:17:55,242
Oh!

304
00:18:03,416 --> 00:18:05,418
(PRINCES GRUNTING)

305
00:18:05,710 --> 00:18:07,671
(FERGUS CHUCKLES)

306
00:18:07,754 --> 00:18:10,340
I look fine, woman! Leave me be!

307
00:18:10,674 --> 00:18:12,008
GUARD: My Lord!

308
00:18:12,092 --> 00:18:15,303
I want to announce the arrival
of the lords...

309
00:18:15,387 --> 00:18:17,430
- Ow!
- Who goes there? Who goes there?

310
00:18:17,514 --> 00:18:19,516
(BAGPIPES PLAYING)

311
00:18:34,155 --> 00:18:36,157
Boy!

312
00:18:36,825 --> 00:18:39,077
(ALL CRY OUT)

313
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:40,745
(SHOUTING)

314
00:18:44,374 --> 00:18:45,375
(SILENCE)

315
00:18:46,334 --> 00:18:49,254
So, here we are... Er...

316
00:18:50,046 --> 00:18:52,215
- ...the four clans.
- MAN: Aye.

317
00:18:52,299 --> 00:18:54,301
- Er... Gathering...
- Oh.

318
00:18:55,093 --> 00:18:57,220
- ...for...
- (DISCONTENTED MURMURS)

319
00:18:57,304 --> 00:19:00,849
- ...the presentation of the suitors.
- ...the presentation of the suitors.

320
00:19:01,099 --> 00:19:03,643
- (ALL CHEERING)
- FERGUS: Clan Macintosh.

321
00:19:03,727 --> 00:19:06,062
MEN: Macintosh!

322
00:19:06,146 --> 00:19:09,649
Your Majesty,
I present my heir and scion,

323
00:19:09,733 --> 00:19:13,236
who defended our land
from the northern invaders,

324
00:19:13,320 --> 00:19:17,490
and with his own sword, Stab Blooder,

325
00:19:17,574 --> 00:19:19,701
vanquished 1,000 foes.

326
00:19:19,784 --> 00:19:21,786
MEN: Macintosh!

327
00:19:23,038 --> 00:19:24,998
- (SCOFFS)
- FERGUS: Clan Mac Guffin!

328
00:19:25,081 --> 00:19:26,750
MEN: Mac Guffin!

329
00:19:27,542 --> 00:19:31,755
Good Majesty, I present my eldest son,

330
00:19:31,838 --> 00:19:34,632
who scuttled the Viking longships

331
00:19:34,716 --> 00:19:39,429
and with his bare hands
vanquished 2,000 foes.

332
00:19:39,679 --> 00:19:41,681
MEN: Mac Guffin!

333
00:19:44,434 --> 00:19:45,685
Clan Dingwall.

334
00:19:45,769 --> 00:19:47,771
MEN: Dingwall!

335
00:19:48,855 --> 00:19:51,941
I present my only son

336
00:19:53,443 --> 00:19:57,530
who was besieged by 10,000 Romans

337
00:19:57,614 --> 00:20:01,868
and he took out a whole armada
singlehandedly.

338
00:20:01,993 --> 00:20:03,453
With one arm, he was...

339
00:20:04,746 --> 00:20:07,415
With one arm he was steering the ship

340
00:20:07,499 --> 00:20:10,627
and with the other
he held his mighty sword

341
00:20:10,710 --> 00:20:13,421
and struck down a whole attacking fleet.

342
00:20:13,505 --> 00:20:15,882
- MAN: Lies!
- What? I heard that.

343
00:20:16,132 --> 00:20:18,134
- (MEN SNICKERING)
- Go on. Say it to my face.

344
00:20:18,468 --> 00:20:21,137
Or are ye scared, simpering jackanapes,

345
00:20:21,221 --> 00:20:23,515
afraid to muss your pretty hair?

346
00:20:23,598 --> 00:20:26,726
- At least we have hair.
- And all our teeth.

347
00:20:26,810 --> 00:20:29,396
(SPEAKS IN THICK ACCENT)

348
00:20:29,479 --> 00:20:31,231
- MAN: Huh?
- (SHEEP BLEATS)

349
00:20:31,314 --> 00:20:34,776
And we don't hide under bridges,
you grumpy old troll.

350
00:20:34,859 --> 00:20:36,820
(ALL LAUGHING)

351
00:20:38,321 --> 00:20:40,448
You want to laugh, huh?

352
00:20:40,740 --> 00:20:42,659
Wee Dingwall!

353
00:20:43,827 --> 00:20:45,954
(SCREAMS) Get off me!

354
00:20:46,204 --> 00:20:47,580
(LAUGHING)

355
00:20:47,664 --> 00:20:48,665
(PLAYING LIVELY TUNE)

356
00:20:48,748 --> 00:20:50,125
(GROANING)

357
00:20:53,753 --> 00:20:54,754
(SCREAMS)

358
00:20:55,839 --> 00:20:57,632
(YELPS)

359
00:20:57,715 --> 00:21:00,176
Nut 'em! Nut 'em! That's the way to...

360
00:21:02,387 --> 00:21:03,555
All right.

361
00:21:05,473 --> 00:21:06,891
Shut it!

362
00:21:07,517 --> 00:21:08,685
(MUSIC WINDS DOWN)

363
00:21:09,227 --> 00:21:13,940
Now, that's all done.
You've had your go at each other.

364
00:21:14,190 --> 00:21:15,859
Show a little decorum.

365
00:21:16,901 --> 00:21:18,945
And no more fighting.

366
00:21:19,195 --> 00:21:20,447
- (MACE CLANGING)
- (SCREAMS)

367
00:21:20,530 --> 00:21:21,531
(LIVELY TUNE CONTINUES)

368
00:21:22,198 --> 00:21:23,199
(YELLING)

369
00:21:29,706 --> 00:21:31,374
(BATTLE CRY)

370
00:21:33,543 --> 00:21:34,544
Ow!

371
00:21:35,670 --> 00:21:36,671
(GROANS)

372
00:21:37,505 --> 00:21:39,299
(SHEEP BLEATS)

373
00:21:39,757 --> 00:21:40,758
(YELLS)

374
00:21:52,270 --> 00:21:54,272
FERGUS: You want a fresh one?

375
00:21:54,522 --> 00:21:56,274
(MUSIC STOPS)

376
00:21:56,357 --> 00:21:58,359
(CLAN CHIEFS WHINING IN PAIN)

377
00:22:00,403 --> 00:22:01,446
FERGUS: Crivens, you're fierce.

378
00:22:01,529 --> 00:22:02,864
I didn't start it. It was...

379
00:22:02,947 --> 00:22:05,617
My lady Queen, I feel terrible.
My humblest apologies.

380
00:22:05,700 --> 00:22:09,287
- We mean no disrespect.
- I'm sorry, love, I didn't... But...

381
00:22:09,370 --> 00:22:11,498
- Yes, dear.
- (CLEARS THROAT)

382
00:22:11,581 --> 00:22:13,333
Now, where were we?

383
00:22:13,416 --> 00:22:17,045
Ah, yes. In accordance with our laws,

384
00:22:17,295 --> 00:22:19,631
by the rights of our heritage,

385
00:22:19,714 --> 00:22:22,967
only the firstborn of each
of the great leaders

386
00:22:23,051 --> 00:22:25,887
- may be presented as champion.
- Firstborn?

387
00:22:25,970 --> 00:22:30,683
And thus compete for the hand
of the Princess of Dun Broch.

388
00:22:31,267 --> 00:22:34,562
To win the fair maiden
they must prove their worth

389
00:22:34,646 --> 00:22:38,816
by feats of strength or arms
in the games.

390
00:22:38,900 --> 00:22:43,530
It is customary that the challenge
be determined by the princess herself.

391
00:22:43,613 --> 00:22:45,323
Archery! Archery.

392
00:22:45,406 --> 00:22:46,616
(ALL MURMURING)

393
00:22:47,784 --> 00:22:51,579
I choose archery.

394
00:22:52,330 --> 00:22:55,500
- Let the games begin!
- (ALL CHEERING)

395
00:23:05,009 --> 00:23:07,470
(GRUNTING)
(YELLS)

396
00:23:11,391 --> 00:23:12,392
(SCREAMS)

397
00:23:12,475 --> 00:23:13,476
(GRUNTING)

398
00:23:15,812 --> 00:23:17,397
Pull!

399
00:23:18,022 --> 00:23:19,857
- Pull!
- (MEN CRYING OUT IN SURPRISE)

400
00:23:19,983 --> 00:23:21,651
(LIVELY BAGPIPES PLAYING)

401
00:23:27,574 --> 00:23:29,576
- (MAN ROARING)
- (CHILDREN SCREAMING)

402
00:23:32,954 --> 00:23:34,956
(MOOING AND BARKING)

403
00:23:36,583 --> 00:23:38,334
- I'll just take one.
- Ooh!

404
00:23:39,586 --> 00:23:41,588
PRINCE: Ooh!

405
00:23:43,131 --> 00:23:44,716
Oh!

406
00:23:44,799 --> 00:23:48,344
Now, I have told you,
you're not allowed... Oh!

407
00:23:49,429 --> 00:23:50,847
- Oh!
- Argh!

408
00:23:51,431 --> 00:23:53,057
- (PRINCES GIGGLING)
- Oh!

409
00:23:56,102 --> 00:23:58,021
(SHEEP BLEATING)

410
00:24:00,898 --> 00:24:02,900
(HORN SOUNDING)

411
00:24:04,902 --> 00:24:07,655
(DOGS HOWL)

412
00:24:07,780 --> 00:24:09,449
(CROWD CHEERING)

413
00:24:09,824 --> 00:24:11,200
It's time!

414
00:24:13,870 --> 00:24:17,123
- Archers, to your marks!
- Aye, archers, to your marks.

415
00:24:17,373 --> 00:24:20,043
And may the lucky arrow find its target.

416
00:24:20,126 --> 00:24:21,753
(FERGUS CHUCKLES)

417
00:24:26,049 --> 00:24:28,051
(EXCITED SQUEALING)

418
00:24:30,386 --> 00:24:32,096
Oi! Get on with it.

419
00:24:38,936 --> 00:24:40,355
CROWD: Ooh. (LAUGHS)

420
00:24:40,438 --> 00:24:41,731
(GROANS)

421
00:24:42,523 --> 00:24:45,693
- Och!
- I bet he wishes he was tossing cabers.

422
00:24:45,777 --> 00:24:48,738
- Or holding up bridges. (LAUGHS)
- Shh!

423
00:24:51,074 --> 00:24:52,825
(GIRLS SQUEAL)

424
00:24:53,785 --> 00:24:54,827
CROWD: Aw...

425
00:24:54,911 --> 00:24:56,079
(YELLS ANGRILY)

426
00:24:56,162 --> 00:24:59,540
At least you hit the target, son.

427
00:24:59,624 --> 00:25:01,084
(CONTINUES YELLING)

428
00:25:01,167 --> 00:25:02,960
Oh, that's attractive.

429
00:25:03,044 --> 00:25:05,046
(CONTINUES WAILING)

430
00:25:06,756 --> 00:25:08,841
- MAN: I got it!
- Good arm.

431
00:25:08,925 --> 00:25:12,011
And such lovely flowing locks.

432
00:25:12,095 --> 00:25:13,721
- Fergus.
- What?

433
00:25:15,890 --> 00:25:17,058
(LAUGHTER)

434
00:25:17,141 --> 00:25:18,142
(GASPS)

435
00:25:22,855 --> 00:25:24,607
Oh, wee lamb.

436
00:25:30,113 --> 00:25:32,782
Oh, come on! Shoot, boy!

437
00:25:33,991 --> 00:25:35,993
- (CROWD CHEERING)
- (LAUGHS IN TRIUMPH)

438
00:25:36,077 --> 00:25:37,912
Well done, lad! Well done.

439
00:25:37,995 --> 00:25:39,997
(STARTS SINGING)

440
00:25:41,457 --> 00:25:43,626
- Feast your eyes!
- (CHIEFS SCREAM)

441
00:25:44,460 --> 00:25:47,213
- That's my boy. (LAUGHS)
- (GAGGING)

442
00:25:47,463 --> 00:25:50,925
Well, that's just grand now, isn't it?

443
00:25:51,008 --> 00:25:53,761
- Guess who's coming to dinner?
- Fergus.

444
00:25:53,845 --> 00:25:56,931
By the way, hope you don't mind
being called Lady Ding...

445
00:25:57,014 --> 00:25:59,016
(WHINES)

446
00:26:04,147 --> 00:26:06,774
- (CROWD GASPS)
- I am Merida.

447
00:26:06,858 --> 00:26:10,069
Firstborn descendant
of Clan Dun Broch.

448
00:26:10,153 --> 00:26:13,656
And I'll be shooting for my own hand.

449
00:26:13,740 --> 00:26:14,866
- Oh!
- (CROWD MURMURING)

450
00:26:15,825 --> 00:26:18,202
What are you doing?

451
00:26:20,955 --> 00:26:22,915
Merida!

452
00:26:22,999 --> 00:26:24,876
Curse this dress!

453
00:26:25,251 --> 00:26:27,253
(SHOCKED GASPS)

454
00:26:31,007 --> 00:26:32,049
(CROWD GASPS IN AWE)

455
00:26:32,175 --> 00:26:33,718
Merida, stop this!

456
00:26:38,014 --> 00:26:40,850
Don't you dare loose another arrow.

457
00:26:47,857 --> 00:26:48,941
(EXHALES)

458
00:26:50,109 --> 00:26:52,278
Merida, I forbid it.

459
00:27:23,059 --> 00:27:25,686
Michty me!
I've just about had enough of you, lass!

460
00:27:25,770 --> 00:27:28,481
- You're the one that wants me to...
- You embarrassed them.

461
00:27:28,564 --> 00:27:30,399
- You embarrassed me.
- I followed the rules.

462
00:27:30,483 --> 00:27:32,360
You don't know what you've done!

463
00:27:32,443 --> 00:27:35,029
- Just don't care how I...
- It'll be fire and sword if it's not set right.

464
00:27:35,112 --> 00:27:37,657
- Just listen!
- I am the Queen!

465
00:27:37,740 --> 00:27:39,283
You listen to me!

466
00:27:39,367 --> 00:27:41,661
Ugh! This is so unfair!

467
00:27:41,744 --> 00:27:43,454
Ha! Unfair?

468
00:27:43,538 --> 00:27:45,581
You're never there for me.

469
00:27:45,665 --> 00:27:48,334
This whole marriage is what you want.

470
00:27:48,417 --> 00:27:51,587
Do you ever bother
to ask what I want? No.

471
00:27:51,671 --> 00:27:54,006
You walk around telling me what to do,
what not to do,

472
00:27:54,507 --> 00:27:57,093
trying to make me be like you.

473
00:27:57,176 --> 00:27:59,470
Well, I'm not going to be like you.

474
00:27:59,554 --> 00:28:01,222
Oh, you're acting like a child.

475
00:28:01,305 --> 00:28:04,141
And you're a beast.

476
00:28:04,225 --> 00:28:06,143
- That's what you are!
- Oh, Merida.

477
00:28:06,227 --> 00:28:08,563
- I'll never be like you.
- No, stop that!

478
00:28:08,646 --> 00:28:11,649
- I'd rather die than be like you!
- (GASPS)

479
00:28:16,279 --> 00:28:18,739
Merida, you are a princess,

480
00:28:18,823 --> 00:28:21,617
- and I expect you to act like one.
- Mum!

481
00:28:23,160 --> 00:28:24,328
Oh!

482
00:28:28,958 --> 00:28:29,959
(WEEPS)

483
00:28:30,042 --> 00:28:32,044
ELINOR: Merida!

484
00:28:33,045 --> 00:28:34,547
Merida!

485
00:28:35,464 --> 00:28:37,383
Oh, dear.

486
00:28:37,466 --> 00:28:39,302
Ah!

487
00:28:41,178 --> 00:28:43,764
Oh, no. What have I done?

488
00:28:45,308 --> 00:28:46,726
Oh.

489
00:28:47,393 --> 00:28:49,395
(SOBBING)

490
00:28:54,483 --> 00:28:56,485
(SOBBING)

491
00:29:13,127 --> 00:29:15,421
Oh! Oh! Oh!

492
00:29:16,088 --> 00:29:17,089
(WHINNIES)

493
00:29:17,673 --> 00:29:19,759
Whoa!

494
00:29:19,842 --> 00:29:22,219
(SOBS) Angus!

495
00:29:22,762 --> 00:29:25,264
(WHINNIES AND SNORTS)

496
00:29:34,190 --> 00:29:36,192
(ANGUS WHINNIES)

497
00:29:47,328 --> 00:29:49,372
(WISP CALLS)

498
00:29:57,672 --> 00:30:00,216
(WISP CALLS)

499
00:30:08,557 --> 00:30:11,560
- (WHISPERS) Come on, Angus.
- (ANGUS NICKERS)

500
00:30:11,644 --> 00:30:12,812
Angus!

501
00:30:12,895 --> 00:30:14,480
(NICKERS)

502
00:30:14,563 --> 00:30:16,315
(SIGHS)

503
00:30:16,899 --> 00:30:18,901
(WISPS CALL)

504
00:30:20,569 --> 00:30:22,405
(ANGUS NEIGHS)

505
00:30:23,572 --> 00:30:25,700
(WISP CALLS)

506
00:30:29,537 --> 00:30:30,663
(WHINNYING)

507
00:30:55,062 --> 00:30:57,064
(WISP CALLS)

508
00:31:01,736 --> 00:31:04,196
Why would the wisps lead me here?

509
00:31:12,913 --> 00:31:14,915
(BELL TINKLES)

510
00:31:15,666 --> 00:31:16,751
Uh...

511
00:31:19,503 --> 00:31:21,505
(WOOD GENTLY TAPPING)

512
00:31:29,346 --> 00:31:31,307
Oh, look around.

513
00:31:31,390 --> 00:31:33,559
You holler if you see anything you like.

514
00:31:33,642 --> 00:31:35,978
Everything is half off.

515
00:31:36,479 --> 00:31:37,521
Uh...

516
00:31:41,358 --> 00:31:44,403
- Who are you?
- Just a humble woodcarver.

517
00:31:44,487 --> 00:31:45,988
Um...

518
00:31:46,280 --> 00:31:48,783
I don't understand... (GASPS)

519
00:31:48,866 --> 00:31:50,993
- See anything you like?
- Uh...

520
00:31:51,285 --> 00:31:55,372
Perhaps a touch of whimsy
to brighten any dank chamber?

521
00:31:55,456 --> 00:31:57,875
But the will-o'-the-wisps, they...

522
00:31:57,958 --> 00:31:59,960
Oh! This is one of a kind!

523
00:32:00,336 --> 00:32:02,004
I'll make you a deal for this rare prize.

524
00:32:04,340 --> 00:32:05,758
- Your broom!
- Oh! (SNAPS)

525
00:32:07,051 --> 00:32:10,054
- It was sweeping by itself.
- That's ridiculous.

526
00:32:10,346 --> 00:32:12,848
Wood cannot be imbued
with magical properties.

527
00:32:12,932 --> 00:32:16,435
I should know. I'm a wit... Whittler.

528
00:32:16,519 --> 00:32:18,270
Of wood.

529
00:32:18,354 --> 00:32:23,609
Oh, how about this conversation starter?
It's made of yew wood.

530
00:32:23,692 --> 00:32:26,028
- (GENTLE CLATTERING)
- Tough as stone.

531
00:32:26,112 --> 00:32:27,488
Oh, ah, ah, ah, ah!

532
00:32:27,571 --> 00:32:29,615
That's stuffed. (LAUGHS)

533
00:32:29,698 --> 00:32:32,952
- Staring is rude.
- (GASPS) Ooh! The crow's talking!

534
00:32:33,035 --> 00:32:34,286
That's not all I can do.

535
00:32:34,370 --> 00:32:36,622
<i>La-la la-la la-la</i>

536
00:32:36,705 --> 00:32:38,582
- (SINGS HIGH NOTES)
- (SNAPS)

537
00:32:40,876 --> 00:32:42,503
(SQUAWKS)

538
00:32:43,045 --> 00:32:45,965
- You're a witch!
- Woodcarver.

539
00:32:46,048 --> 00:32:48,384
That's why the wisps led me here.

540
00:32:48,884 --> 00:32:50,928
- Woodcarver!
- You'll change my fate!

541
00:32:51,011 --> 00:32:53,806
- Woodcarver!
- You see, it's my mother.

542
00:32:53,889 --> 00:32:56,976
I'm not a witch!
Too many unsatisfied customers.

543
00:32:59,395 --> 00:33:04,358
If you're not going to buy anything,
get out. (SNAPS)

544
00:33:04,733 --> 00:33:07,570
- No! The wisps led me here!
- I don't care!

545
00:33:08,737 --> 00:33:13,325
- Get out! Shoo! Get! Be gone with you!
- I'll buy it all.

546
00:33:14,034 --> 00:33:16,620
- What? What was that?
- Every carving.

547
00:33:16,704 --> 00:33:18,372
Well... (STAMMERING)

548
00:33:18,455 --> 00:33:22,751
(LAUGHS) And how are you going
to pay for that, sweetie?

549
00:33:22,835 --> 00:33:25,504
- With this.
- W...

550
00:33:28,090 --> 00:33:31,010
Oh, my, that's lovely, that is.

551
00:33:31,093 --> 00:33:32,428
That would set us up for months.

552
00:33:32,553 --> 00:33:33,554
(CLATTERING)

553
00:33:34,471 --> 00:33:35,848
- MERIDA: Ah, ah, ah.
- (GASPS)

554
00:33:35,931 --> 00:33:41,770
- Every carving and one spell.
- (SQUAWKS)

555
00:33:42,521 --> 00:33:45,482
Are you sure
you know what you're doing?

556
00:33:45,566 --> 00:33:49,111
I want a spell to change my mum.

557
00:33:49,361 --> 00:33:51,655
That'll change my fate.

558
00:33:51,739 --> 00:33:53,032
Hmm... Done!

559
00:33:54,450 --> 00:33:55,910
- (CHUCKLES)
- Where are you going?

560
00:33:55,993 --> 00:33:57,036
(SNAPS)

561
00:33:57,119 --> 00:33:58,704
- (SQUAWKING)
- There.

562
00:33:58,787 --> 00:34:00,122
What are you doing?

563
00:34:00,539 --> 00:34:03,125
You never conjure where you carve.

564
00:34:03,417 --> 00:34:04,793
Very important.

565
00:34:08,547 --> 00:34:10,925
WITCH: The last time I did this
was for a prince.

566
00:34:11,008 --> 00:34:12,551
- (CLAPS)
- (CAULDRON IGNITES)

567
00:34:12,635 --> 00:34:14,887
Easy on the eyes. Tight pants.

568
00:34:14,970 --> 00:34:18,599
He demanded I give him
the strength of ten men.

569
00:34:18,682 --> 00:34:21,936
And he gave me this for a spell.

570
00:34:22,728 --> 00:34:24,688
A spell that would change his fate.

571
00:34:26,607 --> 00:34:28,025
And did he get what he was after?

572
00:34:28,108 --> 00:34:29,735
(LAUGHS) Yes.

573
00:34:29,818 --> 00:34:33,906
And made off with an especially
attractive mahogany cheese board.

574
00:34:33,989 --> 00:34:36,742
Now, what do I need? Oh!

575
00:34:36,825 --> 00:34:38,869
- Just a little bit of this.
- (THUNDER RUMBLING)

576
00:34:38,953 --> 00:34:39,954
Ah. (CHUCKLES)

577
00:34:40,037 --> 00:34:41,038
Hoo!

578
00:34:42,081 --> 00:34:44,583
(SQUAWKING)

579
00:34:44,667 --> 00:34:47,002
Tee-tee-tee-tee. Whoosh.

580
00:34:47,086 --> 00:34:48,837
That'll do.

581
00:34:53,175 --> 00:34:55,177
(HUMS HAPPILY)

582
00:34:56,637 --> 00:34:58,847
- (SQUAWKS)
- Mi-mi-mi-mi-mi-mi-mi.

583
00:35:02,059 --> 00:35:03,060
(BANG)

584
00:35:03,143 --> 00:35:04,937
(PANICKED WHINNYING)

585
00:35:06,563 --> 00:35:12,695
And now let's see. What have we here?

586
00:35:15,739 --> 00:35:17,533
(GASPS) Oh!

587
00:35:18,575 --> 00:35:19,660
- Hey!
- (SQUAWKS)

588
00:35:20,703 --> 00:35:22,538
Uh, a cake?

589
00:35:22,621 --> 00:35:25,624
- You don't want it?
- Yes! I want it.

590
00:35:26,166 --> 00:35:30,254
You're sure if I give this to my mum,

591
00:35:30,546 --> 00:35:32,256
it will change my fate?

592
00:35:32,548 --> 00:35:34,091
Oh. (CHUCKLES)

593
00:35:34,174 --> 00:35:37,469
Trust me. It'll do the trick, dearie.

594
00:35:38,137 --> 00:35:42,975
Expect delivery of your purchase
within a fortnight.

595
00:35:43,058 --> 00:35:45,060
Ooh! Ooh...

596
00:35:45,936 --> 00:35:48,147
What was that thing about the spell?

597
00:35:48,897 --> 00:35:51,817
Did you say something about

598
00:35:52,776 --> 00:35:54,903
the spell?

599
00:35:57,906 --> 00:36:02,911
<i>Mor'du, Mor'du, now the time has
come for all of us to slaughter you</i>

600
00:36:03,662 --> 00:36:04,663
ALL: Hooray!

601
00:36:04,747 --> 00:36:06,582
<i>Mor'du, Mor'du...</i>

602
00:36:07,750 --> 00:36:09,752
(DISTANT SINGING)

603
00:36:24,933 --> 00:36:26,935
- ELINOR: Merida.
- Mum!

604
00:36:27,019 --> 00:36:28,854
Ooh, uh... I, uh...

605
00:36:28,937 --> 00:36:32,024
- Oh, I've been worried sick.
- You... You were?

606
00:36:32,107 --> 00:36:35,652
I didn't know where you'd gone
or when you'd come back.

607
00:36:35,736 --> 00:36:38,614
I didn't know what to think.
Oh, look at your dress.

608
00:36:38,697 --> 00:36:41,575
Oh. Angus threw me. But I'm not hurt.

609
00:36:41,658 --> 00:36:45,788
Well, you're home now,
so that's the end of it.

610
00:36:46,789 --> 00:36:50,125
- Honestly?
- I've pacified the lords for now.

611
00:36:50,209 --> 00:36:53,170
Your father's out there
"entertaining" them.

612
00:36:53,253 --> 00:36:55,047
<i>Come taste my blade, you manky bear</i>

613
00:36:55,130 --> 00:36:56,799
<i>For gobbling up my leg</i>

614
00:36:57,216 --> 00:37:00,928
<i>I'll hunt you, then I'll skin you,
hang your noggin on a peg...</i>

615
00:37:01,011 --> 00:37:02,221
(CHEERING)

616
00:37:03,305 --> 00:37:07,142
Of course, we both know
a decision still has to be made.

617
00:37:11,105 --> 00:37:13,899
- What's this?
- It's a peace offering.

618
00:37:13,982 --> 00:37:17,152
I made it. For you. Special.

619
00:37:17,236 --> 00:37:20,114
You made this for me?

620
00:37:21,824 --> 00:37:22,866
Mm.

621
00:37:25,786 --> 00:37:28,580
Oh. Interesting flavour.

622
00:37:28,664 --> 00:37:31,625
- How do you feel?
- What... What is that?

623
00:37:31,708 --> 00:37:33,335
- Different?
- Mm...

624
00:37:33,585 --> 00:37:36,880
Tart and, um, (GULPS) gamy.

625
00:37:36,964 --> 00:37:40,676
Have you changed your mind at all
about the marriage and all that?

626
00:37:41,677 --> 00:37:43,178
Oh, that's better.

627
00:37:43,262 --> 00:37:45,347
Now, why don't we go
upstairs to the lords

628
00:37:45,681 --> 00:37:48,767
and put this whole kerfuffle to rest?

629
00:37:48,851 --> 00:37:50,185
Hm?

630
00:37:54,648 --> 00:37:56,066
(CELTIC FLUTE MUSIC PLAYING)

631
00:37:56,859 --> 00:37:57,901
Ooh.

632
00:37:57,985 --> 00:38:00,779
- Mother?
- I'm woozy suddenly.

633
00:38:00,863 --> 00:38:03,282
My head's spinning like a top. Ooh!

634
00:38:03,365 --> 00:38:07,119
- Mum!
- Oh, suddenly I'm not so well.

635
00:38:07,202 --> 00:38:11,039
Er... How... How do you feel
about the marriage now?

636
00:38:11,123 --> 00:38:14,126
Merida! Oh, just take me to my room.

637
00:38:14,209 --> 00:38:16,795
FERGUS: All right, that's fine.
That's just fine.

638
00:38:16,879 --> 00:38:20,716
A little to the left. That's good.
A wee bit to the left. That's good.

639
00:38:20,799 --> 00:38:22,259
It's good enough.

640
00:38:22,342 --> 00:38:24,887
Now, clear out of there, boys.
I don't want you to spoil my shot.

641
00:38:25,387 --> 00:38:27,139
- What? (CLEARS THROAT)
- My lady Queen.

642
00:38:27,222 --> 00:38:30,142
We've been waiting patiently.

643
00:38:30,225 --> 00:38:35,230
Milords, I am out of sorts
at the moment.

644
00:38:35,314 --> 00:38:39,109
But you shall have your answer.
(BURPS)

645
00:38:39,193 --> 00:38:40,652
- Oh!
- Eh?

646
00:38:40,736 --> 00:38:42,696
Presently.

647
00:38:42,779 --> 00:38:45,741
Now, if you'll (GROANS) excuse us.

648
00:38:47,409 --> 00:38:48,994
- (ALL CHEERING)
- FERGUS: Elinor, look!

649
00:38:49,077 --> 00:38:51,079
It's Mor'du! (LAUGHS)

650
00:38:52,748 --> 00:38:54,625
Elinor? Are you all right, dear?

651
00:38:54,708 --> 00:38:56,543
Fine. I'm fine.

652
00:38:56,627 --> 00:38:58,879
Go about avenging your leg. Oh...

653
00:38:58,962 --> 00:39:01,006
Aye. You heard her, lads.

654
00:39:01,089 --> 00:39:05,177
I dream about the perfect way
to make this devil die.

655
00:39:05,260 --> 00:39:06,595
(ALL CHEERING)

656
00:39:08,639 --> 00:39:12,601
Just take all the time you need
to getting yourself right, Mum.

657
00:39:12,684 --> 00:39:16,647
Then maybe in a bit you might have
something new to say on the marriage.

658
00:39:16,730 --> 00:39:19,149
What was in that cake?

659
00:39:19,233 --> 00:39:20,817
(SCOFFS) Cake.

660
00:39:20,943 --> 00:39:22,611
(COUGHS)
(GROANS)

661
00:39:23,028 --> 00:39:24,196
Mum?

662
00:39:24,279 --> 00:39:26,949
So I'll just tell them
the wedding's off, then?

663
00:39:27,032 --> 00:39:29,034
(ELINOR GROANING)

664
00:39:32,037 --> 00:39:34,039
Mum?

665
00:39:37,626 --> 00:39:39,628
(DEEP GROANING)

666
00:39:50,055 --> 00:39:51,807
(GASPS)

667
00:39:54,685 --> 00:39:56,979
(SCREAMS)

668
00:39:58,105 --> 00:39:59,356
(LOW GROWLING)

669
00:40:01,066 --> 00:40:02,150
Bear!

670
00:40:03,193 --> 00:40:04,861
(WHINES)

671
00:40:04,945 --> 00:40:06,947
(FRIGHTENED GROWL)

672
00:40:07,030 --> 00:40:08,282
(PANTING)

673
00:40:10,867 --> 00:40:12,953
- (GROWLS)
- (SCREAMS)

674
00:40:21,378 --> 00:40:24,089
(SURPRISED ROARING)

675
00:40:25,966 --> 00:40:26,967
- (GROANS)
- Oh!

676
00:40:36,435 --> 00:40:37,978
Mum?

677
00:40:39,730 --> 00:40:42,983
You're... You're a bear!

678
00:40:44,026 --> 00:40:45,027
(GROANS)

679
00:40:45,110 --> 00:40:46,486
Why a bear?

680
00:40:46,737 --> 00:40:50,741
Oh, that scaffy witch
gave me a gammy spell.

681
00:40:52,784 --> 00:40:54,119
It's not my fault.

682
00:40:54,202 --> 00:40:56,163
I didn't ask her
to change you into a bear.

683
00:40:56,246 --> 00:41:00,876
I just wanted her to change you.

684
00:41:02,252 --> 00:41:03,962
(ROARS)

685
00:41:04,963 --> 00:41:06,840
(ALL CHEERING)

686
00:41:06,923 --> 00:41:09,384
- Shh. Did you hear that? (SNIFFS)
- (MUSIC STOPS)

687
00:41:09,468 --> 00:41:11,720
Something's not right.

688
00:41:11,803 --> 00:41:14,139
(ANXIOUS WHINING)

689
00:41:15,057 --> 00:41:18,352
There's no point in having a go at me.
The witch is to blame.

690
00:41:18,435 --> 00:41:20,812
Goggly old hag.

691
00:41:21,521 --> 00:41:23,982
Eyes all over the place.

692
00:41:24,775 --> 00:41:27,069
- Unbelievable.
- (GROANING)

693
00:41:28,236 --> 00:41:30,822
- I'll get her to fix this.
- (SIGHS)

694
00:41:30,906 --> 00:41:33,533
MERIDA: Why do I always get blamed
for everything? It's just not fair.

695
00:41:34,910 --> 00:41:36,912
(SNIFFING)

696
00:41:36,995 --> 00:41:39,247
Everybody, follow me.

697
00:41:39,331 --> 00:41:41,333
And keep a sharp eye.

698
00:41:42,959 --> 00:41:45,671
Here we go.
Another hunt through the castle.

699
00:41:45,754 --> 00:41:47,422
But we haven't had dessert yet.

700
00:41:47,547 --> 00:41:50,926
(SPEAKS IN THICK ACCENT)

701
00:41:52,761 --> 00:41:54,763
(LAUGHS) I have no idea.

702
00:41:55,764 --> 00:41:58,392
MERIDA: Mum, you can't go out there.

703
00:41:59,434 --> 00:42:01,812
Mum! Wait!

704
00:42:03,438 --> 00:42:07,317
What are you doing?
Dad. The Bear King?

705
00:42:07,401 --> 00:42:09,569
If he so much as sees you, you're dead.

706
00:42:09,820 --> 00:42:13,407
LORD DINGWALL: Another one of
your entertainments to bore us to death!

707
00:42:13,490 --> 00:42:15,033
LORD MACINTOSH:
Oh, and what exactly are we after...

708
00:42:15,117 --> 00:42:16,118
Mum!

709
00:42:16,201 --> 00:42:18,036
LORD MACINTOSH: ...my liege?

710
00:42:18,120 --> 00:42:19,246
LORD MACGUFFIN:
Best to humour him.

711
00:42:19,329 --> 00:42:21,289
He is, after all, the King.

712
00:42:21,373 --> 00:42:22,416
(SNIFFING)

713
00:42:25,210 --> 00:42:27,587
He's like a hound with that nose of his.

714
00:42:27,838 --> 00:42:28,964
(LICKS AND SPITS)

715
00:42:29,047 --> 00:42:30,882
Mum, wait.

716
00:42:30,966 --> 00:42:32,384
- We have to...
- (GROANS)

717
00:42:32,467 --> 00:42:34,845
- (CLATTERING)
- Follow me.

718
00:42:34,928 --> 00:42:36,555
Stop.

719
00:42:36,805 --> 00:42:37,848
Stop!

720
00:42:39,182 --> 00:42:40,183
(GASPS)

721
00:42:41,184 --> 00:42:43,353
You're covered with fur.

722
00:42:43,437 --> 00:42:45,105
You're not naked.

723
00:42:45,188 --> 00:42:47,149
It's not like anyone's gonna see you.

724
00:42:52,154 --> 00:42:53,572
(SCREAMS)

725
00:42:54,489 --> 00:42:56,032
Now you've done it.

726
00:42:56,116 --> 00:42:57,868
(SCREAMS)

727
00:42:58,452 --> 00:43:00,245
Maudie!

728
00:43:00,328 --> 00:43:03,039
- (STUTTERING)
- Just calm down, lass. What is it?

729
00:43:03,123 --> 00:43:05,250
- (STUTTERING)
- Spit it out, Maudie!

730
00:43:05,333 --> 00:43:07,169
(SHOUTING) A bear!

731
00:43:07,252 --> 00:43:08,879
I knew it! (YELLS)

732
00:43:08,962 --> 00:43:10,088
(ALL SHOUTING)

733
00:43:10,172 --> 00:43:11,965
Would you just listen to me?

734
00:43:12,048 --> 00:43:14,926
- We can't go this way. You'll be seen.
- (MEN YELLING)

735
00:43:15,010 --> 00:43:16,303
Quick! This way!

736
00:43:18,680 --> 00:43:19,681
Mum?

737
00:43:25,937 --> 00:43:27,689
(WHIMPERS)

738
00:43:33,111 --> 00:43:34,237
(ALL GASP)

739
00:43:35,906 --> 00:43:37,616
(SOFTLY) Mum? Oh!

740
00:43:37,866 --> 00:43:39,868
(MEN SHOUTING)

741
00:43:43,163 --> 00:43:45,290
- Oh!
- (ELINOR WHINING)

742
00:43:54,299 --> 00:43:55,342
Hm?

743
00:43:56,426 --> 00:43:59,596
A witch turned Mum into a bear.
It's not my fault.

744
00:43:59,679 --> 00:44:02,057
We've got to get out of the castle.
I need your help.

745
00:44:02,599 --> 00:44:04,309
Oh, all right.

746
00:44:04,392 --> 00:44:07,687
You can have my desserts
for two... Three weeks.

747
00:44:09,397 --> 00:44:11,525
Okay. Fine. A year.

748
00:44:17,572 --> 00:44:19,324
- Did you hear that?
- Shh.

749
00:44:19,407 --> 00:44:21,284
(ECHOING ROAR)

750
00:44:23,620 --> 00:44:25,914
(ECHOING ROAR)

751
00:44:27,123 --> 00:44:29,376
- There it goes!
- (MEN SHOUTING)

752
00:44:31,086 --> 00:44:32,504
- (MOCK ROARING CONTINUES)
- FERGUS: Come on, lads!

753
00:44:32,587 --> 00:44:34,422
(YELLS)

754
00:44:36,591 --> 00:44:39,010
- (YELLS)
- (MOCK GROWLING)

755
00:44:40,428 --> 00:44:41,513
There it goes!

756
00:44:43,056 --> 00:44:44,766
(ALL YELLING)

757
00:44:50,105 --> 00:44:51,648
(BIRD CALL)

758
00:44:55,110 --> 00:44:57,404
- Come on, Mum.
- (WHINES)

759
00:44:57,487 --> 00:44:59,406
(CLATTERING)

760
00:45:01,116 --> 00:45:02,367
LORD MACGUFFIN:
Think we should lay a trap?

761
00:45:02,450 --> 00:45:04,160
FERGUS: Try shutting yours!

762
00:45:04,244 --> 00:45:06,204
(ALL ARGUING)

763
00:45:06,288 --> 00:45:07,622
(MOCK GROWLING)

764
00:45:07,706 --> 00:45:09,541
- There he is!
- (MEN SHOUTING)

765
00:45:14,504 --> 00:45:16,256
(ALL SHOUTING)

766
00:45:21,970 --> 00:45:23,638
FERGUS: I'm sure it went this way.

767
00:45:23,722 --> 00:45:25,265
LORD MACGUFFIN:
You can see my house from here.

768
00:45:25,348 --> 00:45:27,267
It must have sprouted wings.

769
00:45:27,350 --> 00:45:30,520
Was carried away by a giant birdy.

770
00:45:30,604 --> 00:45:33,565
- A dragon, perhaps.
- Bear in the castle!

771
00:45:33,648 --> 00:45:36,026
Doesn't make sense.
It cannot open doors.

772
00:45:36,109 --> 00:45:37,986
He's got big giant paws!

773
00:45:38,069 --> 00:45:39,446
Let's just get inside.

774
00:45:40,155 --> 00:45:41,531
(GRUNTING)

775
00:45:41,615 --> 00:45:44,326
- It's locked.
- Dingwall was the last up.

776
00:45:44,409 --> 00:45:46,578
LORD DINGWALL:
I propped it open with a stick.

777
00:45:46,661 --> 00:45:48,330
(MEN GRUMBLING)

778
00:45:52,709 --> 00:45:56,338
HANDMAID: What did you see, Maudie?
Just spit it out, Maudie.

779
00:45:56,421 --> 00:45:58,924
Oh, for goodness' sakes, Maudie,
would you get a grip?

780
00:45:59,007 --> 00:46:00,008
(CLATTERING)

781
00:46:02,344 --> 00:46:04,387
(SCREAMS)

782
00:46:04,471 --> 00:46:06,181
HANDMAID: Maudie, honey, come here!
It's all right!

783
00:46:07,641 --> 00:46:09,184
Come on, Mum. Quick.

784
00:46:10,101 --> 00:46:11,102
(GROANS)

785
00:46:11,186 --> 00:46:12,604
Shh.

786
00:46:18,526 --> 00:46:20,612
(CRASHING AND CLATTERING)

787
00:46:22,197 --> 00:46:24,199
(CLATTERING)

788
00:46:25,450 --> 00:46:27,118
(GIGGLING)

789
00:46:27,410 --> 00:46:28,411
(SNEEZES)

790
00:46:29,245 --> 00:46:30,413
(WHINES)

791
00:46:30,497 --> 00:46:32,290
They'll be fine. Won't you, boys?

792
00:46:32,374 --> 00:46:33,375
(SNIFFS)

793
00:46:33,792 --> 00:46:36,127
Mum, we've got to hurry.

794
00:46:36,211 --> 00:46:37,629
Now, I'll be back soon.

795
00:46:37,712 --> 00:46:41,007
Go on and help yourself
to anything you want, as a reward.

796
00:46:42,801 --> 00:46:44,636
(ALL GASP)

797
00:46:55,230 --> 00:46:57,607
(STRAINING) Oh!

798
00:46:57,691 --> 00:46:58,692
(LORD DINGWALL SIGHS)

799
00:46:58,817 --> 00:47:00,527
Right!

800
00:47:07,659 --> 00:47:09,703
MERIDA: Where are these wisps?

801
00:47:09,786 --> 00:47:13,123
Come out, wisps. Come on out.

802
00:47:14,749 --> 00:47:17,335
Lead me to the witch's cottage.

803
00:47:18,461 --> 00:47:20,463
I'm here!

804
00:47:21,381 --> 00:47:24,968
Fine. Don't come out
now that my mum's watching.

805
00:47:25,051 --> 00:47:26,094
(WHINES)

806
00:47:26,177 --> 00:47:31,182
I was standing right here
and the wisp appeared right there.

807
00:47:31,266 --> 00:47:34,686
Then a whole trail of them
led me off into the forest.

808
00:47:40,775 --> 00:47:45,113
Oh, does she think we're just going
to happen upon the witch's cottage?

809
00:47:46,156 --> 00:47:47,574
(OWLS HOOTING)

810
00:47:53,663 --> 00:47:55,290
(DISTANT HOWLING)

811
00:47:59,127 --> 00:48:01,337
Oh, Mum, I know this place.

812
00:48:01,880 --> 00:48:03,840
The witch's cottage...

813
00:48:04,632 --> 00:48:07,802
It's this way! Come on! Hurry!

814
00:48:17,187 --> 00:48:20,148
I can't believe it. I found it.

815
00:48:20,231 --> 00:48:22,067
(WHINES)

816
00:48:24,694 --> 00:48:27,447
No. She was here.

817
00:48:28,406 --> 00:48:31,576
No, really, she was just here.

818
00:48:31,659 --> 00:48:32,869
(WHINES)

819
00:48:33,161 --> 00:48:34,621
Oh, wait.

820
00:48:39,292 --> 00:48:41,336
- No.
- (BANGS DOOR SHUT)

821
00:48:41,419 --> 00:48:44,839
No, no. No! No!

822
00:48:47,092 --> 00:48:49,177
- (METAL RATTLES)
- Oh.

823
00:48:49,260 --> 00:48:51,513
(RUMBLING)

824
00:48:53,681 --> 00:48:54,766
(DINGING)

825
00:48:57,268 --> 00:48:59,437
(SHRIEKS)

826
00:49:00,355 --> 00:49:02,357
(BUBBLING)

827
00:49:09,781 --> 00:49:12,617
<i>Welcome to the Crafty Carver,</i>

828
00:49:12,700 --> 00:49:16,162
<i>home of bear-themed carvings
and novelties.</i>

829
00:49:16,246 --> 00:49:19,374
<i>I am completely out of stock at this time.</i>

830
00:49:19,457 --> 00:49:24,754
<i>But if you'd like to enquire about
portraits or wedding cake toppers,</i>

831
00:49:24,838 --> 00:49:26,798
<i>pour vial one into the cauldron.</i>

832
00:49:26,881 --> 00:49:29,551
<i>If you'd like the menu in Gaelic, vial two.</i>

833
00:49:29,634 --> 00:49:32,470
<i>If you're that red-haired lass, vial three.</i>

834
00:49:32,554 --> 00:49:34,889
<i>To speak with a live homunculus...</i>

835
00:49:35,557 --> 00:49:39,435
<i>Princess, I'm off to the Wickerman
Festival in Stornoway</i>

836
00:49:39,519 --> 00:49:41,479
<i>and won't be back till spring.</i>

837
00:49:41,563 --> 00:49:45,191
<i>There's one bit I forgot to tell you
about the spell.</i>

838
00:49:45,275 --> 00:49:49,154
<i>By the second sunrise,
your spell will be permanent,</i>

839
00:49:49,237 --> 00:49:53,575
- (GASPS)
<i>- unless you remember these words.</i>

840
00:49:54,576 --> 00:49:56,661
<i>Fate be changed,</i>

841
00:49:56,744 --> 00:49:58,663
<i>look inside,</i>

842
00:49:58,746 --> 00:50:00,665
<i>mend the bond</i>

843
00:50:00,748 --> 00:50:02,792
<i>torn by pride.</i>

844
00:50:02,876 --> 00:50:06,921
"Fate be changed... Mend the bond."
What does that mean?

845
00:50:07,005 --> 00:50:08,673
<i>One more time.</i>

846
00:50:08,756 --> 00:50:10,633
<i>Fate be changed,</i>

847
00:50:10,717 --> 00:50:12,760
<i>look inside,</i>

848
00:50:12,844 --> 00:50:14,637
<i>mend the bond</i>

849
00:50:14,721 --> 00:50:17,265
<i>torn by pride.</i>

850
00:50:17,348 --> 00:50:18,683
<i>That's it. Ta-ta.</i>

851
00:50:18,766 --> 00:50:22,645
<i>Oh, and thank you for shopping
at the Crafty Carver.</i>

852
00:50:22,729 --> 00:50:25,356
No. No! Where'd you go?

853
00:50:25,440 --> 00:50:27,942
<i>- Welcome to the Crafty Carver...</i>
- What?

854
00:50:28,026 --> 00:50:30,236
<i>...for all your...</i>
(SPEECH OVERLAPPING)

855
00:50:30,320 --> 00:50:34,616
Maybe there's a book of spells.
Look around. We'll need more vials.

856
00:50:36,492 --> 00:50:39,537
<i>I'm off to the Wickerman Festival
in Stornoway...</i>

857
00:50:39,621 --> 00:50:41,789
(SCRAMBLED MESSAGES)

858
00:50:42,498 --> 00:50:45,543
<i>Thank you for visiting.
Have a lovely day.</i>

859
00:50:45,627 --> 00:50:46,628
(BANG)

860
00:50:51,424 --> 00:50:53,426
(WHINES SOFTLY)

861
00:51:04,270 --> 00:51:06,189
(RAIN PATTERING)

862
00:51:06,272 --> 00:51:07,482
(MERIDA STRAINING)

863
00:51:18,326 --> 00:51:19,452
(ELINOR SIGHS)

864
00:51:22,538 --> 00:51:24,791
We'll sort it out tomorrow.

865
00:51:43,059 --> 00:51:45,186
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

866
00:51:53,111 --> 00:51:55,113
(FAINT SINGING)

867
00:51:58,574 --> 00:52:00,576
(ELINOR SINGING IN GAELIC)

868
00:52:07,500 --> 00:52:09,711
- (CRACK OF THUNDER)
- (SCREAMS)

869
00:52:10,378 --> 00:52:12,422
Oh. (SPEAKS GAELIC)

870
00:52:13,381 --> 00:52:16,467
My brave wee lassie, I'm here.

871
00:52:16,551 --> 00:52:19,554
I'll always be right here.

872
00:52:21,472 --> 00:52:23,474
(CONTINUES SINGING IN GAELIC)

873
00:52:25,101 --> 00:52:27,103
(BOTH SINGING)

874
00:52:38,740 --> 00:52:40,742
(BIRDSONG)

875
00:52:41,784 --> 00:52:43,953
Uh... Good morning.

876
00:52:44,037 --> 00:52:45,997
(MOANS)

877
00:52:46,080 --> 00:52:48,124
So... (CHUCKLES)

878
00:52:48,416 --> 00:52:51,586
- What's all this supposed to be?
- (SIGHS)

879
00:52:51,669 --> 00:52:53,421
Oh.

880
00:52:53,504 --> 00:52:55,673
(MOANS AND GRUNTS)

881
00:52:55,757 --> 00:52:57,425
What?

882
00:52:57,508 --> 00:52:59,844
(HUFFS AND SNORTS)

883
00:53:04,182 --> 00:53:06,100
Sorry. I don't speak bear.

884
00:53:06,184 --> 00:53:07,226
(HUFFS)

885
00:53:11,189 --> 00:53:12,690
Oh.

886
00:53:13,733 --> 00:53:14,734
(MOANS)

887
00:53:17,487 --> 00:53:18,529
Ah!

888
00:53:18,613 --> 00:53:19,614
(GRUNTS IN SURPRISE)

889
00:53:23,701 --> 00:53:24,702
(SLURPS)

890
00:53:27,121 --> 00:53:29,791
- Find those by the creek, did you?
- Mm-hm.

891
00:53:29,874 --> 00:53:31,250
They're nightshade berries.

892
00:53:31,334 --> 00:53:33,086
Mmm.

893
00:53:33,795 --> 00:53:35,421
They're poisonous.

894
00:53:37,131 --> 00:53:38,132
(SPUTTERING)

895
00:53:43,971 --> 00:53:47,016
Where did you get this water?
It has worms.

896
00:53:50,103 --> 00:53:51,979
(GULPS)

897
00:53:52,980 --> 00:53:54,023
(THUDDING)

898
00:53:54,107 --> 00:53:55,858
(BIRDS SQUAWK)

899
00:53:57,860 --> 00:54:00,780
- (GIGGLES) Come on.
- (GROWLS SOFTLY)

900
00:54:08,830 --> 00:54:09,997
Breakfast.

901
00:54:10,665 --> 00:54:11,749
(GRUNTS APPROVINGLY)

902
00:54:11,833 --> 00:54:16,754
Oh, wait. A princess should not
have weapons, in your opinion.

903
00:54:16,879 --> 00:54:18,589
Uh-huh... (GROANS)

904
00:54:18,673 --> 00:54:20,091
There you go.

905
00:54:21,592 --> 00:54:23,010
Go on.

906
00:54:23,094 --> 00:54:24,971
(GROANS)

907
00:54:25,847 --> 00:54:28,474
How do you know you don't like it
if you won't try it?

908
00:54:28,558 --> 00:54:29,851
(WHINES)

909
00:54:38,484 --> 00:54:39,569
(GROANS APPROVINGLY)

910
00:54:43,948 --> 00:54:45,450
Mm.

911
00:54:46,200 --> 00:54:47,201
(MUNCHING LOUDLY)

912
00:54:53,458 --> 00:54:54,917
(GRUNTS)

913
00:54:55,710 --> 00:54:57,086
(BURPS)

914
00:54:57,170 --> 00:54:58,296
(GROANS)

915
00:54:58,379 --> 00:55:00,131
(SLOW SONG PLAYING)

916
00:55:00,214 --> 00:55:04,635
<i>This love it is a distant star</i>

917
00:55:04,719 --> 00:55:08,848
<i>Guiding us home wherever we are</i>

918
00:55:09,807 --> 00:55:13,936
<i>This love it is a burning sun</i>

919
00:55:14,187 --> 00:55:18,483
<i>Shining light on the things
that we've done</i>

920
00:55:19,400 --> 00:55:25,239
<i>I tried to speak to you every day</i>

921
00:55:25,323 --> 00:55:32,246
<i>But each word we spoke
the wind blew away</i>

922
00:55:36,292 --> 00:55:39,587
<i>How did we let it come to this?</i>

923
00:55:41,005 --> 00:55:42,757
<i>What we just tasted...</i>

924
00:55:42,840 --> 00:55:44,759
(MERIDA LAUGHS)

925
00:55:47,178 --> 00:55:52,683
<i>How will it feel when this day is done?</i>

926
00:55:53,017 --> 00:55:59,982
<i>And can we keep
what we've only begun?</i>

927
00:56:00,650 --> 00:56:01,692
(CRIES OUT)

928
00:56:01,776 --> 00:56:07,448
<i>Could these walls
come crumbling down?</i>

929
00:56:08,616 --> 00:56:14,622
<i>I want to feel my feet on the ground</i>

930
00:56:15,581 --> 00:56:20,378
<i>Can we carry this love that we share</i>

931
00:56:21,504 --> 00:56:26,217
<i>Into the open air</i>

932
00:56:28,511 --> 00:56:34,141
<i>Into the open air</i>

933
00:56:36,477 --> 00:56:37,603
Hey!

934
00:56:39,272 --> 00:56:41,649
Where are you going?

935
00:56:47,280 --> 00:56:52,410
<i>This love it is a burning sun</i>

936
00:56:52,660 --> 00:56:54,954
Mum, come back.

937
00:56:55,037 --> 00:56:56,664
(GROWLS)

938
00:57:01,002 --> 00:57:02,837
- Uh...
- (SNARLS)

939
00:57:02,920 --> 00:57:03,963
- Oh...
- (GROWLING)

940
00:57:07,925 --> 00:57:10,052
Mum, is that you?

941
00:57:11,137 --> 00:57:13,139
(ROARS)

942
00:57:13,222 --> 00:57:15,933
Uh... Mum?

943
00:57:17,643 --> 00:57:19,687
(WHINES)

944
00:57:22,690 --> 00:57:24,692
You changed.

945
00:57:24,775 --> 00:57:26,193
Like you were a...

946
00:57:27,111 --> 00:57:30,573
I mean, like you were a bear
on the inside.

947
00:57:31,032 --> 00:57:33,075
(WHINES AND SNORTS)

948
00:57:39,373 --> 00:57:40,374
(WISP CALLS)

949
00:57:40,458 --> 00:57:41,959
A wisp.

950
00:57:42,043 --> 00:57:44,670
- Mum!
- (WISP SQUEAKS)

951
00:57:44,754 --> 00:57:46,756
Stop it!

952
00:57:47,715 --> 00:57:49,383
Mum, no!

953
00:57:50,593 --> 00:57:51,636
(WISP CALLING)

954
00:57:51,719 --> 00:57:53,721
Mum...

955
00:57:55,014 --> 00:57:56,015
(GRUNTS)

956
00:57:58,559 --> 00:58:01,187
- (GROANS)
- Jings, crivens, help ma boab.

957
00:58:01,270 --> 00:58:03,773
Mum, I know you're scared,

958
00:58:03,856 --> 00:58:06,817
you're tired, you don't understand,

959
00:58:06,901 --> 00:58:10,154
but we've got to keep our heads.

960
00:58:10,237 --> 00:58:12,657
Just calm down.

961
00:58:13,157 --> 00:58:15,159
Listen.

962
00:58:18,871 --> 00:58:19,872
(FAINT WHISPERING)

963
00:58:24,210 --> 00:58:26,212
(FAINT WHISPERING CONTINUES)

964
00:58:34,887 --> 00:58:36,889
(WISP CALLS)

965
00:58:43,646 --> 00:58:45,106
They'll show us the way.

966
00:58:48,067 --> 00:58:50,069
(WISPS CALLING)

967
00:59:00,329 --> 00:59:02,957
(WISP CALLING)

968
00:59:13,384 --> 00:59:15,177
MERIDA: Mum, look.

969
00:59:22,017 --> 00:59:23,185
(WIND WHISTLES)

970
00:59:23,269 --> 00:59:25,146
(ELINOR BEAR GROANS)

971
00:59:25,229 --> 00:59:27,815
MERIDA: Why did the wisps
bring us here?

972
00:59:27,940 --> 00:59:29,442
(ELINOR BEAR MOANS)

973
00:59:34,613 --> 00:59:36,657
(ELINOR BEAR HUFFS AND SNORTS)

974
00:59:54,925 --> 00:59:57,344
Whoever they were,
they've been gone for a long, long time.

975
00:59:57,428 --> 00:59:59,930
(SCREAMS)

976
01:00:01,474 --> 01:00:03,017
(GROANS)

977
01:00:03,100 --> 01:00:05,853
- (WHINES)
- I'm fine, Mum.

978
01:00:05,936 --> 01:00:07,313
Just fine.

979
01:00:16,989 --> 01:00:18,991
It's, uh,

980
01:00:19,867 --> 01:00:20,951
a throne room.

981
01:00:22,745 --> 01:00:24,455
You suppose this could've
been the kingdom

982
01:00:24,538 --> 01:00:26,248
in that story you were telling me?

983
01:00:26,332 --> 01:00:29,168
- (MOANS)
- The one with the princes.

984
01:00:29,710 --> 01:00:31,045
(GROANS)

985
01:00:32,963 --> 01:00:34,548
One,

986
01:00:34,840 --> 01:00:35,925
two,

987
01:00:36,008 --> 01:00:37,468
three,

988
01:00:37,551 --> 01:00:39,386
four.

989
01:00:39,470 --> 01:00:41,347
The oldest.

990
01:00:41,639 --> 01:00:42,640
(GROANS)

991
01:00:44,308 --> 01:00:46,477
Split, like the tapestry.

992
01:00:48,062 --> 01:00:49,063
(GROWLING)

993
01:00:49,146 --> 01:00:50,523
(GASPS)

994
01:00:52,107 --> 01:00:55,444
The spell. It's happened before.

995
01:01:00,032 --> 01:01:02,535
"Strength of ten men."

996
01:01:03,869 --> 01:01:06,080
"Fate be changed."

997
01:01:08,249 --> 01:01:11,126
"Changed his fate."

998
01:01:12,211 --> 01:01:13,838
Oh, no.

999
01:01:13,921 --> 01:01:15,965
The prince became...

1000
01:01:18,801 --> 01:01:20,261
(GROWLING)

1001
01:01:21,846 --> 01:01:23,848
- Mor'du.
- (ROARS)

1002
01:01:23,931 --> 01:01:25,266
(ROARING)

1003
01:01:27,476 --> 01:01:29,103
(SCREAMS)

1004
01:01:33,732 --> 01:01:35,276
(GROANING)

1005
01:01:35,359 --> 01:01:36,986
- (ROARS)
- (FABRIC TEARING)

1006
01:01:41,574 --> 01:01:43,367
- (WHIMPERING)
- (ROARS)

1007
01:01:51,500 --> 01:01:52,501
(SNARLS)

1008
01:01:58,591 --> 01:01:59,633
(MOANS)

1009
01:02:08,851 --> 01:02:10,102
(HUFFING AND PANTING)

1010
01:02:15,983 --> 01:02:17,943
(SCREAMS)

1011
01:02:19,445 --> 01:02:21,488
(CREAKING)

1012
01:02:25,075 --> 01:02:27,202
(MERIDA GROANS)

1013
01:02:29,288 --> 01:02:31,999
Mum, we need to get back to the castle.

1014
01:02:32,625 --> 01:02:35,920
If we don't hurry,
you'll become like Mor'du.

1015
01:02:36,003 --> 01:02:37,379
A bear!

1016
01:02:37,463 --> 01:02:39,632
A real bear. Forever!

1017
01:02:39,882 --> 01:02:43,469
- (WHINES)
- "Mend the bond torn by pride."

1018
01:02:44,261 --> 01:02:47,890
The witch gave us the answer.
The tapestry.

1019
01:02:56,649 --> 01:03:00,361
- (ELINOR GRUMBLES)
- Mum, do you have a better idea?

1020
01:03:01,654 --> 01:03:03,030
(GRUNTS)

1021
01:03:15,292 --> 01:03:16,585
(STRAINING)

1022
01:03:18,629 --> 01:03:20,005
That'll do.

1023
01:03:21,507 --> 01:03:23,509
(TALKING INDISTINCTLY)

1024
01:03:27,554 --> 01:03:29,473
(MEN SHOUTING)

1025
01:03:34,687 --> 01:03:37,356
No more talk. No more traditions.

1026
01:03:37,439 --> 01:03:38,816
We settle this now!

1027
01:03:38,899 --> 01:03:40,484
You're the King.

1028
01:03:40,567 --> 01:03:44,488
You decide which one of our sons
your daughter will marry.

1029
01:03:44,571 --> 01:03:47,658
None of your sons
are fit to marry my daughter.

1030
01:03:47,741 --> 01:03:50,744
Then our alliance is over!
This means war!

1031
01:03:51,912 --> 01:03:53,580
(SHOUTING)

1032
01:03:55,541 --> 01:03:57,209
They're gonna murder each other.

1033
01:03:57,292 --> 01:03:59,753
You've got to stop them
before it's too late.

1034
01:03:59,837 --> 01:04:01,463
(WHINES)

1035
01:04:01,547 --> 01:04:02,965
I know, I know!

1036
01:04:03,048 --> 01:04:05,718
But how do we get you through there
and up to the tapestry

1037
01:04:05,801 --> 01:04:07,845
with the lot of them
boiling over like that?

1038
01:04:08,595 --> 01:04:10,389
- (GRUNTS)
- Oh!

1039
01:04:14,309 --> 01:04:16,478
(SHOUTING)

1040
01:04:22,317 --> 01:04:23,777
(SHOUTING STOPS)

1041
01:04:26,947 --> 01:04:30,534
- What are you doing, lass?
- It's all right, Dad.

1042
01:04:30,617 --> 01:04:33,287
(CLEARS THROAT) I, um...

1043
01:04:34,038 --> 01:04:36,373
I have...

1044
01:04:36,999 --> 01:04:39,918
Well, you see, I...

1045
01:04:40,002 --> 01:04:42,588
I have been in conference
with the Queen.

1046
01:04:42,671 --> 01:04:45,549
- Is that so?
- Aye, it is.

1047
01:04:45,632 --> 01:04:47,885
- Well, where is she, then?
- She, uh...

1048
01:04:47,968 --> 01:04:50,054
How do we know that
this isn't some trick?

1049
01:04:50,137 --> 01:04:51,972
- I'd never...
- This is highly irregular.

1050
01:04:52,056 --> 01:04:53,932
- What are you playing at?
- Where is the Queen?

1051
01:04:54,016 --> 01:04:56,602
LORD MACINTOSH: We will not stand
for any more of this jiggery-pokery.

1052
01:04:56,685 --> 01:04:58,854
- That's right. Let's see her.
- Shut it!

1053
01:04:58,937 --> 01:04:59,938
(SILENCE)

1054
01:05:01,106 --> 01:05:02,232
(LAUGHS)

1055
01:05:02,524 --> 01:05:03,567
(CLEARS THROAT)

1056
01:05:03,650 --> 01:05:05,819
Well, I, uh...

1057
01:05:09,990 --> 01:05:10,991
Uh...

1058
01:05:15,454 --> 01:05:19,083
Once there was an ancient kingdom.

1059
01:05:19,333 --> 01:05:20,959
What is this?

1060
01:05:21,043 --> 01:05:24,588
That kingdom fell into war

1061
01:05:24,671 --> 01:05:26,757
and chaos and ruin...

1062
01:05:26,840 --> 01:05:29,927
Och, we've all heard that tale.
Lost kingdom.

1063
01:05:30,010 --> 01:05:31,595
Aye, but it's true.

1064
01:05:31,678 --> 01:05:35,307
I know now how one selfish act
can turn the fate of a kingdom.

1065
01:05:35,390 --> 01:05:36,767
LORD MACGUFFIN:
Bah, it's just a legend.

1066
01:05:36,850 --> 01:05:38,602
Legends are lessons.

1067
01:05:39,394 --> 01:05:41,480
They ring with truths.

1068
01:05:42,523 --> 01:05:44,108
Our kingdom is young.

1069
01:05:44,358 --> 01:05:46,443
Our stories are not yet legend.

1070
01:05:46,527 --> 01:05:49,655
But in them, our bond was struck.

1071
01:05:49,738 --> 01:05:51,865
Our clans were once enemies.

1072
01:05:51,949 --> 01:05:55,285
But when invaders threatened us
from the sea,

1073
01:05:55,369 --> 01:05:58,372
you joined together to defend our lands.

1074
01:05:58,914 --> 01:06:01,583
You fought for each other.

1075
01:06:01,667 --> 01:06:03,627
You risked everything for each other.

1076
01:06:04,545 --> 01:06:06,964
Lord Mac Guffin, my dad saved your life,

1077
01:06:07,047 --> 01:06:09,591
stopping an arrow
as you ran to Dingwall's aid.

1078
01:06:09,675 --> 01:06:11,468
Aye, and I'll never forget it.

1079
01:06:11,552 --> 01:06:13,220
MERIDA: And, Lord Macintosh,

1080
01:06:13,303 --> 01:06:16,640
you saved my dad
when you charged in on heavy horse

1081
01:06:16,723 --> 01:06:18,433
and held off the advance.

1082
01:06:18,517 --> 01:06:22,563
And we all know how Lord Dingwall
broke the enemy line.

1083
01:06:22,646 --> 01:06:24,690
With a mighty throw of his spear!

1084
01:06:24,773 --> 01:06:26,650
I was aiming at you, you big tumshie.

1085
01:06:26,733 --> 01:06:28,152
(ALL LAUGH)

1086
01:06:28,527 --> 01:06:31,864
The story of this kingdom
is a powerful one.

1087
01:06:31,947 --> 01:06:34,491
My dad rallied your forces

1088
01:06:34,575 --> 01:06:36,952
and you made him your king.

1089
01:06:37,035 --> 01:06:41,123
It was an alliance forged in bravery
and friendship

1090
01:06:41,206 --> 01:06:42,958
and it lives to this day.

1091
01:06:43,041 --> 01:06:45,085
(ALL CHEERING)

1092
01:06:48,547 --> 01:06:51,008
But I've been selfish.

1093
01:06:51,091 --> 01:06:54,136
I tore a great rift in our kingdom.

1094
01:06:54,970 --> 01:06:57,055
There's no one to blame but me.

1095
01:06:57,890 --> 01:07:01,602
And I know now
that I need to amend my mistake

1096
01:07:02,769 --> 01:07:04,438
and mend our bond.

1097
01:07:05,981 --> 01:07:09,818
And so, there is the matter
of my betrothal.

1098
01:07:11,236 --> 01:07:14,531
I've decided to do what's right

1099
01:07:14,615 --> 01:07:15,782
and...

1100
01:07:16,617 --> 01:07:18,243
...and...

1101
01:07:18,952 --> 01:07:20,662
...and...

1102
01:07:21,663 --> 01:07:24,791
...break tradition.

1103
01:07:24,875 --> 01:07:26,335
(GASPING AND MUTTERING)

1104
01:07:31,173 --> 01:07:33,008
My mother...

1105
01:07:34,301 --> 01:07:36,470
...the Queen, feels...

1106
01:07:37,638 --> 01:07:40,807
...uh, in her heart

1107
01:07:40,891 --> 01:07:42,809
that I...

1108
01:07:44,519 --> 01:07:47,189
...that we be free to...

1109
01:07:48,565 --> 01:07:52,152
...write our own story...

1110
01:07:53,904 --> 01:07:58,158
...follow our hearts

1111
01:07:59,117 --> 01:08:02,746
and find love in our own time.

1112
01:08:06,500 --> 01:08:09,586
- That's (SNIFFS) beautiful.
- (ALL SNIFFLING)

1113
01:08:09,670 --> 01:08:13,048
The Queen and I put the decision
to you, my lords.

1114
01:08:13,924 --> 01:08:17,803
Might our young people decide
for themselves who they will love?

1115
01:08:17,886 --> 01:08:18,929
Huh?

1116
01:08:19,012 --> 01:08:22,140
Well, since you've obviously
made up your minds about this,

1117
01:08:22,224 --> 01:08:24,184
I have one thing to say.

1118
01:08:24,268 --> 01:08:26,770
- This is...
- A grand idea!

1119
01:08:26,853 --> 01:08:29,147
Give us our own say
in choosing our fate.

1120
01:08:29,231 --> 01:08:32,567
- What?
- Aye. Why shouldn't we choose?

1121
01:08:32,693 --> 01:08:34,736
But she's the princess.

1122
01:08:34,820 --> 01:08:37,781
I did not pick her out. It was your idea.

1123
01:08:37,864 --> 01:08:41,118
And you... You feel the same way?

1124
01:08:41,201 --> 01:08:46,164
(SPEAKS UNINTELLIGIBLY)

1125
01:08:46,248 --> 01:08:48,667
- Good?
- (GRUNTS)

1126
01:08:48,750 --> 01:08:50,043
(GIGGLES)

1127
01:08:51,336 --> 01:08:52,879
Well, that settles it.

1128
01:08:52,963 --> 01:08:57,676
Let these lads try and win her heart
before they win her hand.

1129
01:08:57,759 --> 01:08:59,094
If they can.

1130
01:08:59,177 --> 01:09:02,139
I say, the wee Dingwall
has a fighting chance.

1131
01:09:02,222 --> 01:09:04,641
Fine, then. Seems for once we agree.

1132
01:09:04,725 --> 01:09:07,769
- It was my idea in the first place.
- (ALL LAUGHING)

1133
01:09:07,853 --> 01:09:09,146
(SIGHS)

1134
01:09:13,025 --> 01:09:15,569
(ALL MUTTERING CONTENTEDLY)

1135
01:09:17,779 --> 01:09:19,656
Just like your mum.

1136
01:09:19,740 --> 01:09:21,033
You devil.

1137
01:09:24,077 --> 01:09:25,078
(GASPS)

1138
01:09:26,705 --> 01:09:29,750
Uh... Everyone to the cellar!

1139
01:09:29,833 --> 01:09:34,254
Let's crack open the King's
private reserve to celebrate!

1140
01:09:34,338 --> 01:09:36,006
(ALL CHEERING)

1141
01:09:36,089 --> 01:09:37,341
Oh.

1142
01:09:37,424 --> 01:09:39,801
(LAUGHS) Whoa, whoa, whoa.

1143
01:09:39,885 --> 01:09:42,054
Psst. Bring the tiny glasses.

1144
01:09:42,137 --> 01:09:44,139
(TALKING AND LAUGHING)

1145
01:09:47,934 --> 01:09:48,977
(SIGHS)

1146
01:09:49,061 --> 01:09:50,437
(MERIDA GIGGLES)

1147
01:09:50,729 --> 01:09:52,773
(SINGS HAPPILY)

1148
01:09:56,109 --> 01:09:57,444
Oh, the tapestry!

1149
01:10:00,238 --> 01:10:02,741
Mend the bond...

1150
01:10:03,950 --> 01:10:06,036
Mend the bond.

1151
01:10:06,119 --> 01:10:08,872
Stitch it up. This'll change you back.

1152
01:10:08,955 --> 01:10:11,291
We just need needle and thread.

1153
01:10:11,416 --> 01:10:12,459
(GRUNTS)

1154
01:10:16,630 --> 01:10:17,672
(GROWLS)

1155
01:10:17,756 --> 01:10:19,841
- Mum?
- (SNARLS)

1156
01:10:21,468 --> 01:10:23,345
Mum? Not now.

1157
01:10:23,428 --> 01:10:26,098
No. Please, not now.

1158
01:10:26,306 --> 01:10:27,307
(SNIFFING)

1159
01:10:27,391 --> 01:10:28,934
- Mum...
- (MEN LAUGHING)

1160
01:10:29,017 --> 01:10:30,268
- (GROWLS)
- Shh.

1161
01:10:32,104 --> 01:10:34,106
(SINGING JOVIALLY)

1162
01:10:37,484 --> 01:10:43,365
Elinor, dear, you'll never guess
who just solved our little suitor problem.

1163
01:10:43,448 --> 01:10:46,660
- (THUNDER RUMBLING)
- (FERGUS BREATHING HEAVILY)

1164
01:10:55,252 --> 01:10:56,586
Elinor!

1165
01:10:59,339 --> 01:11:03,135
It can't be true!
Elinor, answer me, lass!

1166
01:11:03,218 --> 01:11:05,345
Elinor!

1167
01:11:06,430 --> 01:11:08,765
- Merida.
- (SNARLING)

1168
01:11:08,849 --> 01:11:11,143
- What?
- Dad, no! It's not what you think.

1169
01:11:11,226 --> 01:11:13,270
- Merida, get back!
- No!

1170
01:11:13,353 --> 01:11:14,771
(GROWLING)

1171
01:11:15,689 --> 01:11:17,023
(YELLING)

1172
01:11:18,358 --> 01:11:20,444
No, Dad! Don't hurt her!

1173
01:11:21,361 --> 01:11:23,280
- Get out of here!
- (SCREAMS)

1174
01:11:23,363 --> 01:11:25,949
Merida! No!

1175
01:11:26,032 --> 01:11:27,033
(ROARS)

1176
01:11:27,200 --> 01:11:29,035
(YELLS)

1177
01:11:30,078 --> 01:11:32,456
- No!
- (ROARS)

1178
01:11:34,458 --> 01:11:35,750
(MOANS)

1179
01:11:38,628 --> 01:11:40,130
(GROANING)

1180
01:11:40,297 --> 01:11:42,883
- Mum.
- (WHINES)

1181
01:11:44,217 --> 01:11:45,760
(WHIMPERS)

1182
01:11:45,844 --> 01:11:50,724
It's all right. I'm all right. It's nothing.
It's just a little scratch. Mum!

1183
01:11:50,807 --> 01:11:52,767
- My liege!
- (ALL LAUGHING)

1184
01:11:52,851 --> 01:11:54,269
Fergus.

1185
01:11:55,479 --> 01:11:57,147
- Bear!
- (MOANING)

1186
01:11:57,230 --> 01:11:59,274
- (GROANS)
- Dad!

1187
01:11:59,357 --> 01:12:01,902
Count your stars, lass.
It almost had you. Are you hurt?

1188
01:12:01,985 --> 01:12:03,695
It's your wife, Elinor.

1189
01:12:03,778 --> 01:12:05,780
- (ELINOR WHINING)
- (MEN SHOUTING)

1190
01:12:07,574 --> 01:12:08,992
Close the gate!

1191
01:12:12,412 --> 01:12:14,498
- You're talking nonsense!
- It's the truth!

1192
01:12:14,581 --> 01:12:17,792
There was a witch and she
gave me a spell. It's not Mor'du.

1193
01:12:17,876 --> 01:12:20,295
Mor'du or not, I'll avenge your mother!

1194
01:12:20,378 --> 01:12:24,341
- I'll not risk losing you, too.
- MERIDA: No, Dad! Just listen to me.

1195
01:12:24,424 --> 01:12:27,052
Listen! You can't!

1196
01:12:27,135 --> 01:12:31,473
- It's your wife Elinor!
- Maudie, keep this and don't let her out.

1197
01:12:31,598 --> 01:12:34,017
- What about the bear?
- Just stay put.

1198
01:12:34,100 --> 01:12:35,435
(BARKING)

1199
01:12:36,811 --> 01:12:38,939
Oh...

1200
01:12:42,025 --> 01:12:43,693
(YELLING)

1201
01:12:50,492 --> 01:12:51,993
(GRUNTING)

1202
01:12:56,706 --> 01:12:57,707
(STRAINING)

1203
01:13:00,043 --> 01:13:01,044
(FRUSTRATED GRUNT)

1204
01:13:01,294 --> 01:13:03,964
Come on, you sorry bunch of galoots!
Yah!

1205
01:13:12,847 --> 01:13:14,224
Mum!

1206
01:13:14,307 --> 01:13:15,892
No.

1207
01:13:15,976 --> 01:13:17,519
No. Mum.

1208
01:13:20,522 --> 01:13:22,524
(WEEPING)

1209
01:13:35,537 --> 01:13:37,664
(GROANING)

1210
01:13:39,666 --> 01:13:41,084
Maudie. Maudie!

1211
01:13:41,167 --> 01:13:43,795
I need you!

1212
01:13:43,878 --> 01:13:45,338
Now!

1213
01:13:48,341 --> 01:13:50,969
(MERIDA GASPS) Oh, no.

1214
01:13:52,345 --> 01:13:54,264
Maudie.

1215
01:13:57,183 --> 01:13:58,435
(GASPS)

1216
01:13:59,978 --> 01:14:01,021
Get the key.

1217
01:14:08,361 --> 01:14:09,571
(GROWLING)

1218
01:14:09,654 --> 01:14:12,032
(SCREAMING)

1219
01:14:16,703 --> 01:14:17,746
Yah!

1220
01:14:18,038 --> 01:14:20,206
(SCREAMING)

1221
01:14:21,207 --> 01:14:22,584
Oh, Maudie!

1222
01:14:23,793 --> 01:14:24,794
(SCREAMING)

1223
01:14:27,380 --> 01:14:28,757
(BOTH SCREAMING)

1224
01:14:28,840 --> 01:14:31,384
Needle and thread. Needle and thread.
Needle and thread.

1225
01:14:36,056 --> 01:14:37,390
(BARKING)

1226
01:14:39,893 --> 01:14:41,144
(HUFFING AND GASPING)

1227
01:14:44,064 --> 01:14:46,066
(GRUNTS AND MOANS)

1228
01:14:49,611 --> 01:14:51,237
There he goes!

1229
01:14:51,321 --> 01:14:53,990
Needle and thread.
Needle and thread. Needle and thread.

1230
01:14:54,074 --> 01:14:55,325
Ah, you beauty!

1231
01:15:02,332 --> 01:15:04,292
(GASPS)

1232
01:15:04,376 --> 01:15:06,127
(STRAINING)

1233
01:15:11,591 --> 01:15:13,176
(SHRIEKS)

1234
01:15:16,012 --> 01:15:17,931
(GASPS)

1235
01:15:18,264 --> 01:15:19,641
(WHIMPERING)

1236
01:15:22,143 --> 01:15:25,355
One, two... Huh?

1237
01:15:26,272 --> 01:15:27,315
(GASPS)

1238
01:15:29,275 --> 01:15:31,069
- (THUD)
- MAUDIE: Oh!

1239
01:15:31,152 --> 01:15:32,362
(CUB GROWLING)

1240
01:15:32,696 --> 01:15:33,697
(GASPS)

1241
01:15:34,114 --> 01:15:35,115
(WHINING)

1242
01:15:51,464 --> 01:15:53,466
(CRIES OUT)

1243
01:15:54,676 --> 01:15:56,720
Steady, Hamish.

1244
01:15:56,803 --> 01:15:58,805
FERGUS: There he goes.

1245
01:16:00,223 --> 01:16:02,892
- (GRUNTS)
- (DOGS BARKING)

1246
01:16:04,686 --> 01:16:05,729
(GROANS)

1247
01:16:05,812 --> 01:16:07,522
(MEN SHOUTING IN DISTANCE)

1248
01:16:08,940 --> 01:16:10,942
FERGUS: We've got his track!

1249
01:16:11,568 --> 01:16:13,111
- (BARKING)
- (MOANS)

1250
01:16:15,697 --> 01:16:17,866
- Back, back, back!
- Get him!

1251
01:16:18,491 --> 01:16:19,492
(GROANS)

1252
01:16:21,786 --> 01:16:23,788
Angus! Easy, laddie.

1253
01:16:25,206 --> 01:16:26,916
(CRIES OUT)

1254
01:16:27,542 --> 01:16:29,169
Hubert, Harris, help Hamish.

1255
01:16:29,335 --> 01:16:30,336
(SHOUTING)

1256
01:16:30,420 --> 01:16:33,006
FERGUS: Watch your blade!
You're going to take somebody's arm off!

1257
01:16:33,840 --> 01:16:35,175
Aye, we've got you now!

1258
01:16:37,010 --> 01:16:39,387
- FERGUS: Give me a hand over here!
- Put your back into it, Dingwall!

1259
01:16:39,679 --> 01:16:40,805
LORD DINGWALL:
I'm doing all the pulling here.

1260
01:16:40,889 --> 01:16:42,182
LORD MACGUFFIN:
Down you go, you scoundrel.

1261
01:16:45,143 --> 01:16:47,103
